\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-EM stocks ease for sixth day, Philippines c.bank keeps rates steady\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2023\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 MS cuts China's 2023 economic growth forecast to 4.7%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chinese asset manager says will restructure debt\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Philippines c.bank holds rates, ready to resume hikes if needed\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indian c.bank likely sold dollars to support rupee - traders\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 EM stocks ease 0.2%, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  down 0.3%\par \par \uc2 By Bansari Mayur Kamdar\par \par \uc2 Aug 17 (Reuters) - Emerging market stocks headed for a sixth straight day of losses on Thursday, pressured by China's faltering economic growth and possible rate hikes from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 , while the \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its benchmark rate unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso slipped 0.2% against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept interest rates on hold for a third straight meeting.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  too noted that risks to the inflation outlook were skewed to the upside and that food prices were a key concern," said Shivaan Tandon, emerging Asia economist at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 , in a note.\par \par \uc2 "This suggests that the \uc2 BSP (Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas) \uc2 may consider it premature to cut rates before the impact of El Nino becomes clearer given how vulnerable the economy is to such an event."\par \par \uc2 Overall, MSCI's index for emerging market stocks slipped 0.2%, tracking overnight losses on Wall Street after minutes from the Fed's July meeting showed officials were divided over the need for more interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 The EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  index eased 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's benchmark \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  was flat, recouping losses earlier in the session when the index sank more than 2%, while China stocks closed higher, as investors awaited Beijing's stimulus measures that would boost the country's economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks have been under pressure this week as the deepening property crisis and concerns about potential spillover from payment woes of shadow banking-linked trust products weighed on sentiment, along with weak economic data.\par \par \uc2 Faced with a liquidity crisis, Zhongzhi Enterprise Group will conduct a debt restructuring, the Chinese asset manager told investors.\par \par \uc2 China's yuan fell to over nine-month lows against the dollar, as widening yield differentials with the U.S. and expectations of more policy easing by Beijing eclipsed a firmer-than-expected guidance fix and state bank support.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  cut China's economic growth forecast for this year to 4.7%, down from an earlier forecast of 5%.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee weakened against the U.S. dollar, which was supported by U.S. treasury yields, prompting the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hitting a record low, traders said.\par \par \uc2 In central and eastern Europe, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged higher against the euro, while the Hungarian forint slipped 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 The Russian rouble strengthened against the dollar, in a volatile week filled with speculation over how the authorities might stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a 350-basis-point rate hike seemed to have a limited effect.\par \par \uc2 The Vedomosti daily late on Wednesday reported that mandated \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales would not be re-introduced for now and that exporters had informally agreed to raise sales.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand was around flat ahead of the release of business confidence figures later in the day.\par \par \uc2 Global ratings agency \uc2 Fitch\uc2  downgraded Ecuador deeper into junk territory, citing financing risks arising from a significant deterioration in fiscal accounts as the country heads to polls.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Bansari Mayur Kamdar in Bengaluru; editing by Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-17T10:30:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230817ej8h015la\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
