\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 INDIA \highlight\uc2  RUPEE-Rupee weakens but likely \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  keeps losses in check\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2023\par 07:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened against the U.S. dollar on Thursday amid a further rise in US treasury yields, prompting the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a larger decline.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was at 83.10 by 10:46 a.m. IST, compared to Monday's close of 82.9500. Domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were closed on Tuesday and Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was under pressure in the offshore market on Tuesday and Wednesday, but managed to recover on likely \uc2 RBI\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Thursday morning too, \uc2 RBI\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , likely selling dollars via public sector banks to ensure that the rupee did not fall to a record low.\par \par \uc2 There was sizeable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \uc2 RBI\uc2  and the rupee is expected to be in a narrow range for the rest of the day, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a bank said.\par \par \uc2 "While the \uc2 RBI\uc2  has enough \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend a particular level for the rupee, we remain cautious in assuming that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would want to put a hard stop for the pair at 83 level given global pressures," \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2 's treasury research desk said in a note\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $601.45 billion as of August 4, down from $603.87 billion in the week preceding that.\par \par \uc2 Yields on the 10-year U.S. treasury notes rose to 4.2820%, marking the highest level since October 2022.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened against the dollar, with the Malaysian ringgit and Korean won leading losses. The offshore Chinese yuan dropped to an over 9-month low.\par \par \uc2 Major state-run banks in China were seen selling dollars in both offshore and onshore spot markets in a bid to slow down weakness in the yuan. A widening yield differential with the U.S. and economic growth concerns are hurting demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Jaspreet Kalra; Editing by Varun H K) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-17T06:50:52.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230817ej8h00klr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
