\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee's trading volumes, speculative interest plunge as cenbank holds tight\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 8 (Reuters) - Trading volumes and speculative interest in the Indian rupee plummeted over the last several months, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a narrow range, leaving traders with little conviction on future direction.\par \par \uc2 The open interest on USD/INR \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures on the National Stock Exchange (NSE) declined more than 40% to $4.6 billion from this year's peak of near-$8 billion in January.\par \par \uc2 In October 2022, when the rupee dropped to a record low, the open interest had climbed to $8.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee was at 82.80 against the dollar as of 1:30 p.m. IST on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Since February, the rupee held in a less-than-2% range between 81.50-83.00, due to active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when USD/INR moved near either end of the range, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The lack of conviction about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's direction amid the muted volatility dampened volumes and speculative activity.\par \par \uc2 "The size of the position is mainly a function of the conviction on the outlook. And that is missing currently,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nitin Agarwal, India head of trading at ANZ.\par \par \uc2 Average daily volumes on the NSE's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives segment were down more than 30% this month, compared to January levels. Volumes on the NSE represent a large chunk of trading in rupee derivatives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the USD/INR contained to a narrow range, people are not taking large short or long bets. The proprietary activity of banks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  side has reduced," said Ashutosh Tikekar, head of global markets at \uc2 BNP Paribas India\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Instead, banks are focused on managing clients' \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows, he added.\par \par \uc2 Volumes between banks in the over-the-counter segment also witnessed a sizeable decline, mirroring the NSE.\par \par \uc2 The average daily volume so far this month is at $4.5 billion on the interbank order matching system, compared with $6.9 billion in January.\par \par \uc2 "The shrinking range means stop-losses and take-profits are now smaller, both on an intraday and a larger time frame," a senior proprietary trader at a private sector bank said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora and Jaspreet Kalra; Editing by Janane Venkatraman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-9T09:38:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230809ej8900xvh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
