\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee to remain under pressure following dollar index up move\b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is expected to struggle at the opening on Wednesday in the wake of the dollar index's move higher on weak risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards indicate rupee will open slightly weaker to the U.S. dollar from 82.8275 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 "If you take into account the current level, it is to be expected that incremental moves higher (on USD/INR) will be quite slow and measured," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a bank said.\par \par \uc2 "USD/INR longs, which we do not think are too many, may not like this measured pace, but will take comfort that 83 is just right there."\par \par \uc2 The rupee over the last couple of sessions has repeatedly taken support at around 82.80-82.85, which a few market participants reckon is due to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar index climbed 0.5% on Tuesday, helped by the drawdown on U.S. equities. China's disappointing trade data and a downgrade of U.S. mid-sized banks hurt risk sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cut the credit ratings of 10 small- to mid-sized U.S. banks and placed six large lenders on review for potential downgrades on strains from higher funding costs and rising risks.\par \par \uc2 Investors now await the U.S. inflation data due Thursday. On Wednesday, China put out its inflation numbers, which showed that deflation risks were building.\par \par \uc2 "Unless the upcoming U.S. inflation data is way different from consensus, USDINR could stick to the current range for some more time," said Srinivas Puni, managing director at QuantArt Market Solutions.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  policy decision is due at 10:00 a.m. on Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to make no changes to the policy rate but will retain the hawkish tone amid the recent jump in food prices.\par \par \uc2 KEY INDICATORS: ** One-month non-deliverable rupee forward at 82.92; onshore one-month forward premium at 8 paisa ** USD/INR NSE August futures settled on Monday at 82.9250 ** USD/INR August forward premium at 5.5 paisa ** Dollar index at 102.48 ** Brent crude futures down 0.1% at $86 per barrel ** Ten-year U.S. note yield at 4.02% ** As per NSDL data, foreign investors bought a net $272.2mln worth of Indian shares on Aug. 7\par \par \uc2 ** NSDL data shows foreign investors sold a net $7mln worth of Indian bonds on Aug. 7 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Dhanya Ann Thoppil) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-9T03:58:26.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230809ej89008n5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
