\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Low rupee volatility lulls Indian firms into hedging less\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2023\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee's plummeting volatility, mainly due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stranglehold on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is leading both importers and exporters to hedge less of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure.\par \par \uc2 This, in turn, means companies run the risk of being caught off-guard when volatility picks up, exacerbating swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A measure of the rupee's expected volatility over the next one year is hovering at 5.1%, its lowest since 2008. The expected volatility over the next month is down to just 3%, more than half of what it was in October when the rupee hit a record low.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 30-day annualized realized volatility has been under 3% for most of the last three months.\par \par \uc2 "When a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is less volatile, exporters and importers are less willing to hedge their exposure," said Arun Bansal, executive director at \uc2 IDBI Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to data from clearing house CCIL, hedging by importers from January to June dropped almost 12% year-over-year, while hedging by exporters declined 14%.\par \par \uc2 The trend was more pronounced in July, when hedging by importers declined 24%, based on the daily average, and by a steeper 28% for exporters, according to CCIL, whose forward hedging data has a two-day lag.\par \par \uc2 Importers will be reluctant to pay the forward premium to hedge when the rupee is trading in a narrow range, said Bansal.\par \par \uc2 "There is a cost to hedging (for importers) which, while currently around its 10-year low, is still positive," said Nitin Agarwal, heading of trading for India at ANZ.\par \par \uc2 For exporters, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  provide "comfort that a large appreciation on the rupee is unlikely, taking away the urgency to hedge," Agarwal said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's low forward premium, along with the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's reserve rebuilding, has exporters reconsidering their hedges.\par \par \uc2 "The sideways movement in USD/INR has reduced the tendency to hedge," said Anshul Chandak, head of treasury at \uc2 RBL Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Plus, exporters have been on the sidelines for long due to sustained lower forward premiums which have been below 2% on an annualised basis for a very long period now."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  has regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold the rupee in a narrow range. It has mopped up much of the $18 billion inflows into Indian equities since April, which has helped swell India's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $30 billion to above $600 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $15 billion in the spot market in April and May. It is yet to publish data for June.\par \par \uc2 The current low-hedging environment on the back of the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  susceptible to bigger swings when volatility ultimately picks up.\par \par \uc2 For instance, from July to September 2022, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  was intent on not allowing the rupee to depreciate below 80 against the dollar. When the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  did breach that level, it plunged more than 3.5% in the space of a month.\par \par \uc2 "Periods of low volatility and narrow (trading ranges) breed complacency," said \uc2 Anindya Banerjee\uc2 , head of research for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rates at \uc2 Kotak Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "And, when there is a breakout, you see one-sided and disproportionate moves."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Savio D'Souza)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-31T08:04:19.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230728ej7s013w5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
