\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee drops on position adjustments, premiums decline on US yields\b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2023\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee declined on Friday, pressured by the resurgent dollar and position adjustment by speculators, while premiums dropped following a rise in U.S. yields.               \par \par \uc2 The rupee was at 82.2650 to the U.S. dollar by 11:22 a.m. IST, down from 81.93. If rupee's decline holds up, it would mark the worst session in just under two months.               \par \par \uc2 "There has been a rally on the dollar index, but that I do not think is enough to explain today's fall (in rupee)," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trader said.               \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the short dollar positions are opting out."               \par \par \uc2 The rupee had earlier in the week hit around 81.70, where it once again saw \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could be weighing on speculators holding dollar short positions, traders said.               \par \par \uc2 The dollar index inched up in the Asia session, adding to Thursday's rally.  The euro's plunge following the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy outcome and the upbeat U.S. data propped the dollar index to near 101.70.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ECB\uc2  raised rates by 25 basis points, along expected lines, but fanned talks of a September pause. Meanwhile, the U.S. June quarter GDP data was better-than-expected and initial jobless claims dropped to the lowest level since February.               \par \par \uc2 "Following a round of US economic data and a higher probability for a pause in September by \uc2 ECB\uc2 , tables have turned in favour of the dollar," said Kunal Kurani, associate vice president at Mecklai Financial.               \par \par \uc2 "Rupee could travel towards 82.80 levels by August."               \par \par \uc2 U.S. yields rose on Thursday, pushing rupee premiums lower. The 1-year implied yield was down to 1.68%.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-28T06:56:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230728ej7s00ob1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
