\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee ends lower on possible importer demand; Fed in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2023\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BENGALURU, July 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened on Wednesday as importers bought dollars ahead of the month-end, while investors also covered short-dollar positions ahead of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's policy outcome due later in the day.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 81.9950 against the dollar, compared to its previous close of 81.8700.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the had rupee touched 81.6650, its highest since early May, but dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 pushed it back.\par \par \uc2 RBI\uc2 's persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climb back above $600 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are more vulnerable for any hawkish surprise from FOMC than dovish guidance," said Arnob Biswas, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research head at SMC Global.\par \par \uc2 Chances of another rate increase in November have grown to about 34%, versus 26% a week ago, according to the \uc2 CME\uc2 's FedWatch tool.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed before a certain Fed rate hike later in the day, which investors bet will likely be the last for the current rate hike cycle, mainly driven by a fall in the U.S. inflation.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index fell 0.2% to 101.13 ahead of the Fed outcome, but has recovered from a 15-month trough of 99.549 hit a week ago.\par \par \uc2 "It looks far too early for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soften up its FOMC statement by embracing recent disinflationary trends. This should see the dollar holding onto some of its modest gains made over the last week," ING analysts said in a note. (Reporting by Sethuraman NR in Bengaluru; Editing by Varun H K) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-26T11:17:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230726ej7q01hjt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
