\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee gains for second week on inflows, focus shifts to Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2023\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose for a second straight week, helped by foreign inflows into equities, but gains were capped on expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate significantly.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 81.9450 to the U.S. dollar at 3:30 p.m. IST compared with 81.9850 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 0.1% this week, but largely hovered around 82 per dollar amid a lack of volatility. The rupee had risen 0.6% last week.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a rare phase for the rupee where normal influences are not working - be it global or domestic," said Jayram Krishnamurthy, co-founder at Almus Risk Consulting.\par \par \uc2 That, Krishnamurthy said, was due to the actions of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbing the rupee's volatility and showing a clear intent to not let it appreciate, despite many factors working in favour of its rise. Foreign investors bought around $640 million in Indian equities in the first three trading sessions of this week, data from the National Securities Depository Limited showed.\par \par \uc2 Despite the flows, the rupee did not appreciate above 81.95 during the week on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 Focus has now shifted to the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's policy decision due next Wednesday, where a 25 basis point (bps) interest rate hike is completely factored in.\par \par \uc2 Investors will watch out for commentary from Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  next week on the outlook for future rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 A slew of important data releases out of the U.S. - flash purchasing manager's index, June-quarter gross domestic product, initial jobless claims, and core personal consumption expenditures index will also be on investors' radar next week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index is up over 1% so far this week, while the 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield has risen about three bps. (Reporting by Siddhi Nayak; Editing by Sonia Cheema) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-21T11:22:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230721ej7l019lr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
