\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee to track yuan's slide at open, eyes 82.20/USD\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2023\par 04:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is expected to decline on Wednesday, pressured by the yuan's fall on worries over China's growth outlook.\par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards indicate the rupee will open at 82.08-82.12 to the U.S. dollar, compared with 82.03 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 With the yuan "back to losing ways", the rupee will struggle at the open, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 "Anyway, (USD/INR) was not managing to slip below 82 and now we have an excuse to take it to the 82.20-82.30 resistance."\par \par \uc2 The rupee has repeatedly failed to scale the 82 handle despite equity inflows, thanks to likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to traders.\par \par \uc2 They estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set a floor for USD/INR at 81.80-81.90.\par \par \uc2 The offshore Chinese yuan dropped to 7.2140 to the dollar, headed for its fourth straight day of declines, on persistent pessimism regarding the Chinese economy.\par \par \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , on Tuesday, became the latest Wall Street brokerage to lower its forecast for China's 2023 economic growth. On Monday, \uc2 J.P.Morgan\uc2 , \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  and \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  had trimmed their forecasts.\par \par \uc2 Tracking the yuan, most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined. The dollar index managed to inch higher to 100.\par \par \uc2 U.S. data on Tuesday was a tad weaker than expected, with retail sales increasing 0.2% on-month in June, versus 0.5% expected, while industrial production fell a further 0.5%.\par \par \uc2 The data, however, did not impact risk appetite or bond yields. The S&P 500 index rose to its highest since April 2022 and the 2-year U.S. yield inched up to 4.75%.\par \par \uc2 The next important event is the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's meeting next week. A 25 basis points rate hike has been fully priced in.\par \par \uc2 KEY INDICATORS:\par \par \uc2 ** One-month non-deliverable rupee forward at 82.18; onshore one-month forward premium at 8 paisa\par \par \uc2 ** USD/INR NSE July futures settled on Tuesday at 82.07\par \par \uc2 ** USD/INR July forward premium at 3 paisa\par \par \uc2 ** Dollar index up at 100.05\par \par \uc2 ** Brent crude futures down 0.2% at $79.5 per barrel\par \par \uc2 ** Ten-year U.S. note yield at 3.78%\par \par \uc2 ** As per NSDL data, foreign investors bought a net $61.4 million worth of Indian shares on July 17\par \par \uc2 ** NSDL data shows foreign investors bought a net $23.8 million worth of Indian bonds on July 17 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-19T03:44:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230719ej7j008py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
