\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  slip on firm dollar, Thai baht hits 7-month low\b0\par\par\uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2023\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Thai baht hits lowest since Nov. 30\par     \par \par         * \par       South Korean won slips 0.5%\par     \par \par         * \par       Equities in the region mixed\par     \par \par   \par     By Nausheen Thusoo\par        June 28 (Reuters) - Most Asian emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par on the backfoot against a firm dollar on Wednesday, as resilient\par U.S. data eased growth concerns, while the Thai baht hit a\par seven-month low as political uncertainty sparked an investor\par sell-off.\par     Equities in the region were largely mixed, with shares in\par South Korea, down 0.7%, leading declines, while\par Singapore and Malaysia gained 0.1% and 0.3%,\par respectively.\par     The baht depreciated as much as 0.8% to hit its\par lowest level since Nov. 30, as doubts linger over whether the\par leading prime ministerial candidate could secure enough votes to\par assume the top position in the new parliament's first session\par next week.\par     "There seems to be some conflicts between the Pheu Thai\par party and the Move Forward party in terms of the House\par speakership which could lead to more uncertainty about forming\par the coalition government" said Poon Panichpibool, markets\par strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     This could lead to volatility or more weakness for baht in\par July, Panichpibool added.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost 2.2% so far this year, making it one\par of the worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Southeast Asia.\par     The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday it would further\par relax \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulations in the second half this year\par to encourage capital outflows as baht continues to be volatile.\par     Elsewhere, the South Korean won fell 0.5%, while\par the Philippine peso and Singapore dollar slipped\par 0.2% each.\par     In the United States, data showed consumer confidence\par increased in June to the highest level in nearly 1-1/2 years,\par indicating the economy remained on solid footing despite fears\par of a recession.\par     "Despite all the headwinds and a banking sector scare, there\par still is momentum in the U.S. economy," analysts at DBS said in\par a note, adding, it does not look like the U.S. is slipping into\par recession any time soon.\par     "It probably makes sense to trade as if there is no imminent\par recession, noting that the Fed is also poised to tighten at a\par slower pace ahead (which also reduces the risks of an\par accident)."\par     The Chinese yuan inched down 0.1% despite the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the country growing increasingly uncomfortable\par with the recent slide in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     However, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alvin Tan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital\par Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  was\par rather "very obvious" and the deviation from the expected level\par was not very. \par     Markets in Indonesia, and the Philippines\par  were closed for a public holiday.\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Profits at China's industrial firms tumbled 18.8%\par year-on-year in the first five months of 2023\par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as\par ringgit losses 'excessive'\par     ** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 10-year benchmark yields fell 1.1\par basis points to 7.052%\par     \par   Asia stock indexes and                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0724 GMT                             \par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   INDE  STOCKS  STOCKS\par                       DAILY %  YTD %     X   DAILY   YTD %\par                                                  %  \par  Japan                  +0.04  -8.96  <.N2   2.02   27.20\par                                       25>           \par  China     <CNY=CFXS    -0.11  -4.63  <.SS    0.00    3.24\par            >                          EC>           \par  India                  -0.02  +0.83  <.NS    0.80    4.77\par                                       EI>           \par  Indonesi                   -  +3.84  <.JK       -   -2.76\par  a                                    SE>           \par  Malaysia               -0.09  -5.70  <.KL    0.24   -7.05\par                                       SE>           \par  Philippi               -0.19  +0.83  <.PS       -   -0.97\par  nes                                  I>            \par  S.Korea   <KRW=KFTC    -0.54  -3.27  <.KS   -0.67   14.66\par            >                          11>           \par  Singapor               -0.18  -0.86  <.ST    0.10   -1.31\par  e                                    I>            \par  Taiwan                 -0.11  -1.1