\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Thai baht at 7-month low on political uncertainty, equities mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2023\par 06:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Thai baht hits lowest since Nov.30, 2022\par     \par \par         * \par       South Korean won descends 0.3%\par     \par \par         * \par       Equities in the region mixed  \par     \par \par   \par     By Nausheen Thusoo\par        June 28 (Reuters) - The Thai baht weakened to a seven-month low on\par Wednesday as political uncertainty dampened investor appetite, while most other\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also depreciated against a firmer dollar after\par resilient U.S. data eased recession concerns.\par     Equities in the region were largely in the red, with shares in Seoul\par taking the biggest hit, declining 0.8%, while those in the Philippines\par and China lost 0.3% and 0.5%, respectively.\par     The baht depreciated 0.6% to hit its lowest level since Nov. 30,\par 2022 as doubts linger over whether the leading candidate could secure enough\par votes to become prime minister in the new parliament's first session next week.\par     "It is unlikely that the (Move Forward) coalition has the necessary votes to\par go ahead to form a new government," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alvin Tan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The political stalemate and uncertainty in Thailand would drag on if the\par country does not get a new government by next week, Tan added. \par     The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday it will further relax \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulations in the second half this year to encourage capital outflows\par as baht continues to be volatile. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost 2.2% so far this year.\par     Elsewhere, the South Korean won fell 0.3%, while the Philippines\par peso and Singapore dollar slipped 0.2% and 0.1%, respectively. \par     In the United States, data showed consumer confidence increased in June to\par the highest level in nearly 1-1/2 years, indicating the economy remained on\par solid footing despite fears of a recession.\par     "All major data in the U.S. definitely raises bets that there is a\par possibility of the U.S. Fed hiking interest rates again in July and that they\par will not be cutting the interest rates quickly this year also," added Tan. \par     The Chinese yuan inched up 0.04% after signs that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has grown increasingly uncomfortable with the recent slide in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \par     Markets in Indonesia and Philippines were closed for a\par public holiday.\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:    \par     ** Profits at China's industrial firms tumbled 18.8% year-on-year in the\par first five months of 2023\par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as ringgit losses\par 'excessive'\par     ** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 10-year benchmark yields up marginally at 7.069%\par \par     \par  Asia stock                                                    \par  indexes and                                                   \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                                     \p