\par\par \b \uc2 Bankers eye cenbank response to plunge in Indian rupee premiums\b0\par\par\uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2023\par 07:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 31 (Reuters) - Indian rupee premiums are expected to continue to fall, thanks to the surge in U.S. yields, unless the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conducts sell/buy swaps, three bankers said.\par \par \uc2 The implied yield on the dollar/rupee 1-year forward premium plunged to 1.73% on Tuesday. The yield, which hit a low of 1.60% last year, was down more than 50 basis points in May.\par \par \uc2 "The move is predominantly driven by U.S. rates over the last two weeks," Ashutosh Tikekar, head of global markets at \uc2 BNP Paribas India\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 "We could see a knee jerk reaction to 1.6% on the 1-year if we see a further up-move (in short-maturity U.S. yields)."\par \par \uc2 Low premiums discourage exporters to hedge future \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  receipts, bringing down the supply of dollars, while providing an incentive for importers to hedge, leading to higher demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2 This makes the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's job of managing the rupee exchange rate more challenging, a senior trader at a private sector bank, who did not want to be named because he is not allowed to speak to media, said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee declined to 82.85 last week, just about 0.6% away from record low.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 RBI\uc2  will not allow premiums to remain depressed, despite interest rate differentials justifying it," a proprietary trader at another bank, who did not want to be named because of internal policies, said.\par \par \uc2 "And the way I see it, the \uc2 RBI\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the only way premiums can move higher."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  can push premiums higher by conducting USD/INR sell/buy swaps. Last year, when the 1-year premium had dropped to 1.60%, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had done these swaps aggressively via public sector banks, according to several traders.\par \par \uc2 BNP's Tikekar reckons \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in swaps will be contingent on factors other than the level of forward premiums.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 RBI\uc2  has used \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards for sterilization and liquidity management and they will continue to be guided by the same principal rather than just targeting forward levels," Tikekar said.\par \par \uc2 Near-maturity U.S. yields have surged in wake of investors pricing in a higher probability of a Fed rate hike next week and reassessing the likelihood of rate cuts this year. Odds of rate hike next week have risen to 2-in-3.\par \par \uc2 The 1-year U.S. yield is hovering near 5.30%, the highest level since 2001. Meanwhile, the 364-day India Treasury bill yield is near 6.90%.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Nivedita Bhattacharjee) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-31T06:16:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230531ej5v00lwy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
