\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee to see more losses on hawkish Fed, \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  likely\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2023\par 04:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is expected to extend its decline on Friday, weighed by a rising dollar index and U.S. yields following hawkish comments from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials.\par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards indicate rupee will open at around 82.70-82.75 to the U.S. dollar compared with 82.60 in the previous session. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is near the lowest level in almost two months.\par \par \uc2 "Expect RBI (\uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  right at the open," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot trader said. "Highly doubt that \uc2 RBI\uc2  will allow a move above 82.80-83.00 (on USD/INR). That would just make it all the worse for the rupee at a time when it is already under significant pressure."\par \par \uc2 USD/INR overnight swap rate will be a key factor to watch besides the \uc2 RBI\uc2 , he added. The overnight swap rate posted a sizeable decline, which traders said was likely due to a cash dollar shortage.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index inched higher in Asia to add to Thursday's rally, reaching its highest level since mid-March.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined, with the Chinese yuan once again leading the way. The offshore yuan dropped to 7.0750 to the dollar, a level last seen in December.\par \par \uc2 Higher U.S. yields boosted demand for the dollar. The 2-year U.S. yield climbed to 4.28% on comments by Fed officials and U.S. labour market data.\par \par \uc2 Two Fed policymakers said on Thursday that U.S. inflation does not look like it is cooling fast enough to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pause its interest-rate-hike campaign.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the number of Americans filing new claims dropped more than expected, suggesting a resilient labour market.\par \par \uc2 "The current strength of the labour market does not support the Fed's view that the unemployment rate will lift to 4.5% by year-end," ANZ said in a note\par \par \uc2 The odds of a Fed rate hike in June rose to more than 30%.\par \par \uc2 KEY INDICATORS: ** One-month non-deliverable rupee forward at 82.86; onshore one-month forward premium at 8.5 paisa ** USD/INR NSE May futures settled on Thursday at 82.5975 ** USD/INR May forward premium at 2 paisa ** Dollar index up at 103.55 ** Brent crude futures up 0.5% at $76.3 per barrel ** Ten-year U.S. note yield at 3.64% ** SGX Nifty nearest-month futures up 0.2% at 18,210 ** As per NSDL data, foreign investors bought a net $97.8mln worth of Indian shares on May. 17\par \par \uc2 ** NSDL data shows foreign investors bought a net $182.5mln worth of Indian bonds on May. 17 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; editing by Eileen Soreng) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-19T03:53:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230519ej5j00akl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
