\par\par \b \uc2 Bullish view on Indian rupee thwarted by wall of cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2023\par 07:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 15 (Reuters) - The bullish outlook on the Indian rupee that several foreign banks have is facing a tough test from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up reserves.\par \par \uc2 Back in March, analysts from at least three foreign banks projected that the rupee is likely to rally against the U.S. dollar this fiscal year thanks to the improving dynamics in India's current account.\par \par \uc2 India's fiscal year runs from April 1 to March 31.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  projected the rupee to hit 80 per dollar by next March, while \uc2 BofA Securities\uc2  expected a move to 79.5 by then. \uc2 Citi\uc2  said rupee will move to 80 in 6-12 months.\par \par \uc2 The rupee currently is down slightly from its March 31 level, at 82.34 to the dollar. This is despite a resurgence in equity portfolio inflows and the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  signalling a conditional pause. In April and May so far, foreigners have poured $4.5 billion into Indian equities. \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senior treasury officials at public sector banks argue that the call for a stronger rupee is unlikely to materialise as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  mops up inflows to build reserves and keep the local unit in a narrow range.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unlike foreign and private banks, state-owned banks rarely make \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  projections publicly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  could keep leaning against any decline on USD/INR pair to build up reserves, an assistant general manager at a public sector bank through which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said, pointing to the recent price action.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The banker reckons that the overall range for the rupee will "keep shrinking" and that the USD/INR pair will not fall below the 81 levels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is little doubt that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  will persist with its two-way \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy to keep a check on the rupee volatility, chief dealer at another public sector bank said. The rupee is likely to be in the 81.50-82.50 range, the dealer said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2 's dollar purchases have helped lift India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to $596 billion, the highest in almost a year, according to the latest data published by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The reserves had dropped to $524 billion in October.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought about $8 billion in the spot market in November-February, according to data from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Data beyond February is not yet available, but based on the changes in the weekly data, economists said that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains a buyer of dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Broadly, I agree with what the public sector banks are saying, that \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  reckons the need to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and build reserves," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Abheek Barua\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HDFC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBI\f28 \uc2 \f2  probably has a level in mind for the rupee relative to what it thinks is its fair value and in terms of maintaining India's competitiveness."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barua does not expect the rupee to strengthen past 81 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Dhanya Ann Thoppil) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-17T06:04:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230517ej5h00kr9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
