\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee ends little changed on likely dollar buying by \uc2 RBI\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2023\par 12:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 8 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee held in a tight range on Monday with intermittent dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 limiting any upside in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a broadly weaker greenback.\par \par \uc2 The rupee closed at 81.7950 per U.S. dollar compared with 81.80 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 RBI\uc2  is still there in the market... otherwise there is no bidder (for dollars) in the market," a trader with a state-run bank said, adding that exporters were also hedging their dollar receivables at these levels.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been absorbing a large part of the dollar inflows seen in the market over the past week, traders and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 RBI\uc2  continued buying... thus protecting the dollar and exporters from a fall in value," said Anil Kumar Bhansali head of treasury at Finrex Treasury Advisors LLP.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves surged to a 10-month high of $588.8 billion in the week ending April 28, latest data showed. Though the data also accounts for valuation changes, analysts said a large part of it could also be due to dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Foreign institutional investors bought shares worth 116.31 bln rupees ($1.42 bln) in April on a net basis; $1.7 bln over the last six sessions alone.\par \par \uc2 The dollar began the week under pressure on Monday, with traders betting it might have peaked along with U.S. interest rates while keeping a wary eye on looming inflation and loans data.\par \par \uc2 The focus now shifts to U.S. inflation data due Wednesday, with economists expecting a 0.4% month-on-month increase in the core inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 The data will draw scrutiny in the wake of increasing confidence that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will opt to pause its rate.\par \par \uc2 Traders will also watch out for India's inflation data, due later in the week, which will provide cues on the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's next rate hike moves. (Reporting by Nallur Sethuraman in Mumbai; Editing by Janane Venkatraman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-8T11:31:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230508ej5801dx9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
