\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 INDIA \highlight\uc2  RUPEE-Rupee ends nearly flat on likely \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2023\par 12:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 4 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was little changed at close on Thursday in a holiday-shortened week, as likely dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offset foreign inflows into the domestic equity market.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 81.80 compared with 81.8175 in the previous session despite the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  changing its forward guidance to indicate a conditional pause.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 likely stepped in to cap the rupee's sporadic upside through the week, traders said.\par \par \uc2 There were dollar bids from oil marketing companies seen on Thursday, two traders said.\par \par \uc2 "The Indian rupee continues to behave in a range-bound manner, thanks to the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But an improving balance of payments position bodes well in the medium-term, although gains will likely be limited," John Bromhead, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist and macro economist at ANZ, said at the Reuters Global Markets Forum on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 For the week, the rupee fell 0.03% to the dollar and was in a range of 81.945 to 81.66. India's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were off on Monday and are shut again on Friday for a local holiday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index recovered slightly on Thursday after falling 0.6% in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Indian equities received inflows worth 33.35 billion rupees ($407.71 million) this week as of Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Markets did not price in a significant surprise over rate hikes by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  compared with previous meetings, said \uc2 Anand James\uc2 , Chief Market Strategist at \uc2 Geojit Financial Services\uc2 , as he pointed towards the rupee's subdued reaction despite the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hinting at pausing its aggressive tightening cycle.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce its rate decision later in the day. Market positioning is for a 25 basis point hike, though it reflects a chance of a 50 bps increase.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 81.7975 Indian rupees) (Reporting by Nallur Sethuraman and Nimesh Vora in Mumbai; Editing by Sohini Goswami) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-4T11:35:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230504ej54020gd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
