\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee falls, but holds important technical levels; premiums rise\b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2023\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee declined against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, as concerns over a European lender dented broader risk sentiment, but managed to remain on the stronger side of a past resistance level of 82.80.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 82.73 per dollar, against its previous close of 82.5950.\par \par \uc2 Traders said foreign and state-run banks sold dollars around the 82.80-level. Some even reckoned the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem depreciation in the rupee, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has protected those levels in the past.\par \par \uc2 Still, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure to weaken past the 82.80-83 zone, traders added more long positions on USD/INR futures as they expected risk sentiment to remain fragile.\par \par \uc2 "There are higher chances of 83 getting breached and the rupee weakening now," said Jigar Trivedi, senior research analyst, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities at Reliance Securities.\par \par \uc2 There is likely going to be a lot of safe-haven dollar demand due to the turmoil in global markets, Trivedi added.\par \par \uc2 Asian shares declined, while the Chinese yuan and the Indonesian rupiah eased on fears of a banking crisis in U.S. and Europe.\par \par \uc2 Swiss lender \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  tanked on Wednesday after its largest shareholder said it could not provide further support to the bank. The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to come to the rescue to prevent a wider contagion.\par \par \uc2 This came on the heels of U.S lender \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 's collapse.\par \par \uc2 These market events have made investors reassess the size of the rate hikes from central banks in Europe and the U.S. at their upcoming meetings.\par \par \uc2 ECB\uc2  policymakers meet later in the day and earlier bets of a 50 basis point (bps) have been scaled back.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, U.S. bond yields recovered, with 2-year yield trading at around 4.024% after falling to 3.9750% overnight. Rupee premiums rose, with the 1-year yield firming as much as 2.40% to a six-week peak. (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi; Editing by Varun H K) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-3-16T11:28:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230316ej3g01xwp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
