\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 INDIA \highlight\uc2  RUPEE-Rupee ends near 82/USD as likely \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caps gains\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2023\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee strengthened against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, with traders citing inflows, but the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped further gains and brought the local unit closer to 82 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The rupee finished at 81.9750 per dollar, against its previous close of 82.055.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed to 81.7750 during the session, after which traders cited dollar buying by state-run banks, possibly on behalf of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The amount of inflows we're seeing shows the rupee could strengthen up to 81.50 or beyond, but we have to see if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow it, a trader said.\par \par \uc2 Several dealers said dollar inflows by foreign banks have been seen over the past two trading days.\par \par \uc2 The month of March, being the final one in the fiscal year tends to see increased capital inflows and may also be helping the rupee, which has already outperformed its Asian counterparts over the past month.\par \par \uc2 Asian emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were subdued on Thursday as Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's comments this week that rates may need to move higher and potentially hiked faster soured sentiment.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision would rely on upcoming economic data, Powell said, but markets have already pushed up the odds of the Fed reverting to a 50 basis points (bps) rate hike at this month's meeting to 76%.\par \par \uc2 The Fed peak rate expectations have reached 5.65%.\par \par \uc2 "The market, therefore, is likely to keep a close eye on non-farm payrolls report due on Friday and any upward surprise in job addition, the unemployment rate or hourly wage growth could increase the possibility of a 50 bps rate hike," \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  economists wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 "We see the rupee trading in the range of 82.00-82.50 this week." (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi; editing by Eileen Soreng) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-3-9T11:14:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230309ej3901n9d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
