\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee down for the month on hawkish Fed outlook, \uc2 RBI\uc2  limits losses\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2023\par 11:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee advanced against the dollar on Tuesday but was down for the month on worries over U.S. interest rates rising more and staying higher for longer.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 82.6650 to the U.S. dollar on the last day of the month, up from 82.8350 in the previous session. For the month, however, the rupee was down 0.9%.\par \par \uc2 The change in expectations around how many more rate hikes the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  will deliver pressured the rupee and other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February. The better-than-expected U.S. jobs data coupled with upbeat retails and hotter inflation readings prompted investors to reassess the outlook on the Fed funds rate.\par \par \uc2 With U.S. inflation showing little sign of slowing, the Fed mantra of ongoing hikes will continue with 25 bps moves in March, May and June fully priced by markets, \uc2 ING Bank\uc2  said in a note this week.\par \par \uc2 At the beginning of this month, investors had priced in a peak Fed rate of under 5% and around 50 basis points of rate cuts this year. Futures are currently pricing in a peak rate of 5.40% and less than 10 bps of rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 U.S. yields have jumped and the dollar has recovered. The 2-year U.S. yield climbed 80 bps in February, helping lift the dollar index by 2.5%.\par \par \uc2 While the rupee declined in February, it fared much better than its Asian peers, thanks to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar rose 3% against the offshore yuan, and rallied more than 7% versus the Korean won and the Thai baht.\par \par \uc2 "It seems the (Indian) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains super active and is not eager to see the USDINR fly to a new all-time high," \uc2 Anindya Banerjee\uc2 , head of research - \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rates at \uc2 Kotak Securities\uc2 , said. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; editing by Eileen Soreng) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-28T11:22:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230228ej2s024xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
