\par\par \b \uc2 Counting on \uc2 RBI\uc2  support, offshore investors build Indian rupee crosses positions - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2023\par 09:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Foreign investors are wagering that the Indian rupee will do well against other non-U.S. dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the non-deliverable forward market, thanks to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee will hold up better in an environment where the dollar is likely to receive support from the hawkish \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 , they said.\par \par \uc2 Buying the rupee against other non dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "looks straightforward to us with the narrative on the Fed having changed," an analyst at a Singapore-based asset management company, who did not want to be named on account of the fund's policies, said.\par \par \uc2 "You are basically taking a call on the relative volatility, betting that the Fed risks will be least felt on the rupee on account of the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's reaction function."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  has been managing the rupee by building reserves during periods when the dollar is weakening and drawing on reserves when the dollar is rallying, according to analysts.\par \par \uc2 They said the rupee did not participate much in the dollar's decline against its major peers and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from November to January, likely on account \uc2 RBI\uc2 's dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  bought more than $8 billion dollars in the spot market in November and December, according to data by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Data for January was not yet available.\par \par \uc2 Now, with U.S. jobs and inflation data points helping the dollar rally over the last three weeks, the rupee has barely budged on back of the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's dollar sales, held in a narrow 25-paisa range against the dollar this week.\par \par \uc2 Traders have said it was likely the \uc2 RBI\uc2  was not allowing the rupee to weaken past 83.\par \par \uc2 Ashish Agrawal, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and EM macro strategy research, Asia, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said what the \uc2 RBI\uc2  is doing is actively depressing \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk premiums and "ensuring that the modest demand for dollars is satisfied by their selling."\par \par \uc2 "Last year they did look a little persistent at 80 levels and now they are looking a little persistent at 83 levels."\par \par \uc2 Apart from \uc2 RBI\uc2 , another reason for adding a short cross/INR trade is seasonality, the first analyst, from a Singapore-based asset management company, said.\par \par \uc2 Three major research houses - \uc2 BofA Securities\uc2 , \uc2 Citi\uc2  and \uc2 Nomura\uc2 , have said in recent days that rupee should strengthen into the end of India's fiscal year-end, helped by dollar inflows. India's fiscal year runs from Apr. 1 to March 31.\par \par \uc2 "Market in NDFs has been putting large sized cross INR trades like the Korean won/Indian rupee (KRWINR) short and Euro/Indian rupee (EURINR) short," another portfolio fund manager at an Asia-focussed hedge fund, who could not be named on account of the fund's policies, said.\par \par \uc2 He said that these trades were made in the 1-month tenor and that needed two separate legs involving USD/INR and USD/KRW or USD/EUR to take an exposure. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Nivedita Bhattacharjee) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-24T09:37:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230224ej2o01kk5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw