\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-U.S. yields, weak Asian peers fail to disturb the calm on rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2023\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee held a narrow range against the dollar on Wednesday, despite surging U.S. yields and a fall in Asian peers, helped by a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee last traded at 82.85 to the dollar, only marginally lower from 82.79 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened on a flat note and intraday held an about six paisa range despite the overnight jump in U.S. yields.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the non-deliverable forward market and the onshore market to ensure the rupee does not weaken below the 82.90-83 level, according to traders.\par \par \uc2 This has helped keep the rupee in a narrow range and perform better than other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee's Asian peers came under pressure on Wednesday after U.S. yields overnight witnessed another move higher.\par \par \uc2 U.S. yields have been persistently rising on back of the ongoing reassessment on how high the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  could raise rates.\par \par \uc2 Futures are pricing in a peak Fed rate of 5.35% and less than 20 basis points (bps) of rate cuts in the year.\par \par \uc2 An at least 25 bps rate hike at the next two Fed meetings has been fully priced in and there is a high likelihood of a third hike.\par \par \uc2 The recent U.S. economic activity and inflation have signalled that the Fed is likely to remain hawkish.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, data showed U.S. business activity unexpectedly rebounded in February, reaching its highest level in eight months.\par \par \uc2 Focus now turns to the minutes of the last Fed meeting.\par \par \uc2 "Note that the minutes were prepared before the string of firm US data got released and may not be as hawkish as recent Fed speak nor match up to current market pricing," DBS Group Research said in a note. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Sohini Goswami) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-22T11:08:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230222ej2m01ta1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
