\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee's expected volatility at 7-mth low, tracking narrow spot range\b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2023\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee's expected volatility against the dollar over the next one month hit its lowest level in almost seven months on Tuesday, tracking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent narrow trading range and on expectations of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continued support.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's one-month at-the-money volatility was quoting at 4.50/4.80%, near its lowest level since late July last year.\par \par \uc2 The slide in the OTC (over-the-counter) volatility comes alongside a plunge in realized volatility \u8211\'20\'13 measured in terms of the last ten days' closing price \u8211\'20\'13 to 2.2%, its lowest this year.\par \par \uc2 The rupee initially sold off after a much better-than-expected U.S. jobs report on Feb. 3. But, since then it has held in a narrow range of 82.35-to-82.90 with the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening past 83.\par \par \uc2 "The one-month and near-term vols (volatility) have seen the highest impact," said a derivatives trader at a private sector bank, declining to be named due to the bank's internal policies.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's expected near-term volatility is the lowest among major Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah's one-month volatility is near 7.5%, the offshore Chinese yuan's at 6%, and at around 10% on the Thai baht and the Korean won.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants reckon the rupee's implied volatility mostly should be sold.\par \par \uc2 "Rupee usually has been a short volatility trade as realised vols underperforms implied volatility," Ashutosh Tikekar, head of global markets, India, at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "Very rarely would you see a long volatility trade perform, especially at the shorter end."\par \par \uc2 The trader mentioned earlier said a short vols trade at current levels given the hawkish repricing of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's rate path is "a bet that solely relies upon the \uc2 RBI\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-21T09:41:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230221ej2l01i0h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
