\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 INDIA \highlight\uc2  RUPEE-Rupee marks weekly fall; likely \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  limits losses\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2023\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee declined for the fourth straight week on Friday on concerns over surging U.S. yields, but did not weaken below a key level on likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 in the non-deliverable forward (\uc2 NDF\uc2 ) market.\par \par \uc2 The rupee finished the week at 82.83 per dollar, compared with 82.7175 in the previous session. For the week, it was down 0.4%, having traded in a narrow 30 paisa range.\par \par \uc2 However, the rupee's losses for the week were lesser than that of its Asian peers. The Korean won and the Thai baht posted a weekly decline of more than 2%. The Philippine peso dropped 1.5% and the Chinese yuan lost 1%.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  was likely selling dollars in the \uc2 NDF\uc2  market this week, possibly to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening past the 83-level being watched by market participants. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had defended that level back in December.\par \par \uc2 It is "almost a fact" now that if the rupee falls below 83, we will see a record low quite quickly and it will not stop there, a trader at a private sector bank said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's consistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the 83.00 level and the favourable seasonality factors can help a modest recovery of the rupee, Jayaram Krishnamurthy, head of research and advisory at Almus Risk Consulting, said.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were pressured this week by the rise in Treasury yields and the dollar index. The 2-year U.S. yield reached its highest level since November on the back of U.S. data that supported more Federal Reserve rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Fed comments are now turning more hawkish. Two Fed officials said on Thursday the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have lifted interest rates more than the 25 basis points it did at its last meeting. They warned that additional hikes in borrowing costs are essential to lower inflation back to desired levels. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Janane Venkatraman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-17T11:28:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230217ej2h01met\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
