\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee rises on likely dollar inflows, gains in Asian peers\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2023\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 25 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, helped by likely dollar inflows and gains in most major Asian peers.\par \par \uc2 The rupee last traded at 81.59 per U.S. dollar, compared with 81.72 in the previous session. It was a choppy session, with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in a range of 81.50 to 81.76.\par \par \uc2 Rupee bulls can take a lot of positives from today's session - the rupee managed to hold above the 81.80 levels and it arrested the downside momentum, a trader at a Mumbai-based bank said.\par \par \uc2 There was talk of dollar inflows related to \uc2 Adani Enterprises\uc2  and once again, there was good demand from importers, he added.\par \par \uc2 Adani Enterprises\uc2 ' follow-on public offering (FPO) opens on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A tussle between buyers and sellers is likely to continue with inflows pertaining to Adani FPO on one side and the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the other side, said Amit Pabari, managing director at CR \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  likely bought dollars on Monday when the rupee rose above the 81 level, according to traders.\par \par \uc2 The offshore Chinese yuan rose to 6.7750 to the dollar and the Korean won advanced, helped by a fall in Treasury yields. The two-year U.S. yield dropped to near 4.14%.\par \par \uc2 U.S. bonds have rallied this year on bets that softening inflation and growth concerns will force the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to cut interest rates later this year. A 25 basis points rate hike next week by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been priced in.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Indian equities suffered their biggest fall in over a month and futures pointed to a weaker opening for U.S. shares. Oil prices inched up after Tuesday's more than 2% fall. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Shinjini Ganguli) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-1-25T11:18:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230125ej1p01db7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
