\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Traders, corporate position adjustments piles pressure on rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2023\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee declined against the dollar on Tuesday, prompted by speculators and corporates squaring positions on expectations that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside is likely capped, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was quoting at 81.6250 per U.S. dollar by 10:50 a.m IST, compared with 81.39 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reached near 80.90 in Monday, before reversing course on likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The unexpectedly quick reversal is leading to both speculators and corporates having a re-look at their positions, said a trader at a Mumbai-based bank said.\par \par \uc2 Any expectations that the rupee could be poised for a bigger move upwards have faded for now at least, he added.\par \par \uc2 The "Upside for the rupee is capped by \uc2 RBI\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and higher crude oil prices," Mecklai Financial said in a note.\par \par \uc2 While dollar inflows may help to press the USD/INR pair lower, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  will be there to ensure rupee does not appreciative significantly, it said.\par \par \uc2 It pointed to potential dollar inflows from the \uc2 Adani Enterprises\uc2  follow-on public offering that opens this Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's Asian peers were mixed on Tuesday, with the Indonesian rupiah rallying and the offshore Chinese yuan slightly lower. The dollar index was marginally lower, hovering near 102.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  rate decision is due next week, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widely expected to opt for a 25-basis-points rate hike. Softer-than-expected U.S. inflation readings alongside weak data have prompted traders to revisit the Fed expectations. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-1-24T06:37:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230124ej1o00i59\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
