\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee's threat to slip below 83/USD likely nipped by cenbank\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2023\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee declined against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, fuelled by the dollar's surge versus its major peers and importer hedging, though the \uc2 Reserve bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the drop short of the 83-per-dollar mark.\par \par \uc2 The rupee closed at 82.8800 per U.S. dollar, down from 82.7375 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank order matching system fell to 82.9950, prompting state-run banks to sell dollars, likely on behalf of the \uc2 RBI\uc2 , three traders told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with its action in recent trading sessions, which traders suspect led to the rupee repeatedly finding support near the 82.90 level.\par \par \uc2 "(The) \uc2 RBI\uc2  is not allowing it (USD/INR) to move higher and therefore it is unable to cross 83.00 for the present," said Anil Bhansali, head of treasury at Finrex Treasury Advisors.\par \par \uc2 The 83.05-level should be a stop-loss for unhedged positions of importers, he added.\par \par \uc2 The rupee which was anyway under pressure on account of importer hedging was further hurt by the dollar's surge against its major peers. The dollar index rose almost 1%.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index will be eyeing the slew of key U.S. economic data as it seeks to recover from the near 8% decline in the last quarter. U.S. ISM manufacturing and services data is due later this week, alongside the monthly jobs report.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's jump came despite the relatively upbeat risk appetite and the fall in Treasury yields. European shares climbed 1.5% and U.S. equity futures were up about 1%.\par \par \uc2 Investors are focussed on the outlook for global growth following aggressive rate hikes by major central banks. This week's U.S. data will help investors gauge how growth is holding up and the likely path for U.S. interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, it was a choppy session for rupee premiums, with the 1-year implied yield trading in a 1.95% to 2.02% range. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-1-3T11:31:11.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230103ej13018g2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
