\par\par \b \uc2 India should hike rates carefully, prepare for headwinds, \uc2 IMF\uc2  says\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2022\par 15:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, Dec 23 (Reuters) - India's future interest rate hikes should be carefully calibrated and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should be limited to managing volatility, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 has raised its key policy rate by 225 basis points since May, taking the rate to the highest in over three years.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation pressures have led to an appropriate shift towards policy tightening," \uc2 IMF\uc2  said in an annual consultation report. The report is prepared by \uc2 IMF\uc2  staff in accordance with its Article IV of Agreement, which requires the fund to hold annual consultations with officials from member states about economic development and policies.\par \par \uc2 "Additional tightening should be carefully calibrated and communicated," it added.\par \par \uc2 Last week, minutes of the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's monetary policy meeting showed a majority of rate-setters were concerned about elevated inflation and felt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not afford to prematurely pause its rate tightening cycle.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  projected inflation at 6.9% for the current fiscal year that ends on March 31, 2023 and said price gains would moderate gradually.\par \par \uc2 The world's fifth-largest economy is broadly tipped to outperform its major global peers in the year ahead, supported by pent-up post-pandemic domestic demand, investment and credit growth, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  expects India's economic growth to moderate reflecting a less favourable outlook and tighter financial conditions, projecting 6.8% growth for the current fiscal year and 6.1% for the next fiscal year that starts on April 1.\par \par \uc2 "Uncertainty around the outlook is high, with risks tilted to the downside," the Washington-based fund said.\par \par \uc2 A sharp global growth slowdown in the near-term would affect India through trade and financial channels.\par \par \uc2 It projected the current account deficit to widen to 3.5% of GDP in the current fiscal year as a result of both higher commodity prices and import demand.\par \par \uc2 The fund said the exchange rate should act as a "shock absorber" and that the \uc2 RBI\uc2  should only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to address disorderly market conditions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves had fallen around $100 billion from its peak of October 2021, but have since recovered partially due to the resumption of dollar inflows.\par \par \uc2 Fiscal consolidation should be more ambitious than the current baseline, targeting additional general government primary consolidation of around 1% of GDP by 2027/28, the report said. The government is targeting a fiscal deficit of 4.5% of GDP by 2025/26. It does not have a 2027/28 target.\par \par \uc2 It said the government can reverse tax cuts on fuel and phase out support to vulnerable groups through the existing transfer system. India has spent nearly $47 billion for its food programme since April 2020.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  also said other pandemic related schemes such as government credit guarantees for small industries can be unwound.\par \par \uc2 "In the short-term, fiscal consolidation would also support the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's efforts to maintain price stability," the fund said. (Reporting by Shivangi Acharya Nikunj Ohri; Writing by Aftab Ahmed in New Delhi; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-23T15:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221223eicn023rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
