\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee premiums may stay above 2% after \uc2 RBI\uc2 's push - analysts\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2022\par 08:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee's forward premiums could rise further after the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  through public sector banks lifted them from multi-year lows, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The 1-year USD/INR implied yield was at 2.08% on Wednesday, hovering near its highest level in about a month. The yield is up about 45 basis points (bps) from its decade low hit on the day of policy outcome on Dec. 7.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  looks comfortable with the current level of forward premiums, especially since it has lifted informal restrictions on banks for trading in the non-deliverable forward (\uc2 NDF\uc2 ) market, said the treasury head of a private lender, who declined to be named.\par \par \uc2 Premiums are likely to stay elevated going forward, he said, adding that the \uc2 RBI\uc2  is getting comfortable with higher levels of premiums.\par \par \uc2 The low premiums (prior to \uc2 RBI\uc2 's policy decision date)reflected cash dollar shortage which is likely to get alleviated, \uc2 RBI\uc2  Deputy Governor \uc2 Michael Patra\uc2  said at a news conference after the monetary policy review.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  has been conducting sell/buy swaps via public sector banks to lift premiums since the policy date, mostly in far forwards, according to traders.\par \par \uc2 Further, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has removed restrictions on local banks to trade in the \uc2 NDF\uc2  market, helping push premiums higher.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 RBI\uc2  permitting banks to resume offshore-onshore arbitrage resulted in forwards continuing to get paid," said Abhishek Goenka, chief executive of IFA Global. "Banks received \uc2 NDF\uc2  points and paid onshore," Goenka said.\par \par \uc2 The rise in premiums increases the cost of hedging for importers and makes it more attractive for exporters to hedge for the same level of spot, helping the \uc2 RBI\uc2  in managing the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The premiums were overly suppressed and now the bias is "slightly uppish," and this is good from the rupee point of view, said Sajal Gupta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates at Edelweiss Financial Securities.\par \par \uc2 An improvement in dollar liquidity, thanks to \uc2 RBI\uc2 's sell-buy swaps, is supporting higher premiums. The USD/INR overnight swap rate has increased to 0.45-0.50 paisa, after having dropped to 0.33-0.35 paisa earlier this month. The implied rupee yield on USD/INR overnight swap rate is on par with the domestic call money rate.\par \par \uc2 A sell/buy swap involves selling dollar for the spot date and buying them back at a premium at a fixed future date. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Dhanya Ann Thoppil) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-21T08:33:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221221eicl00zq5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
