\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee marginally lower, PSU banks help limit losses - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2022\par 06:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was a tad lower to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, with dollar sales by public sector banks saving the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from bigger declines.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was quoting at 82.8375 per dollar by 10:20 a.m. IST, compared with 82.76 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 While public sector banks are on the offer (on USD/INR), it is unclear whether it's for their books or for the \uc2 RBI\uc2 , a spot trader at a private lender said. However, the price action suggests that the \uc2 RBI\uc2  is not there, the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in USD/INR on either side to manage rupee's level and volatility.\par \par \uc2 The rupee and most of its Asian peers struggled on concerns that hawkish central banks may fuel an economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday raised rates by 50 basis points, but like the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 , signalled the need for more hikes to deal with the inflation threat. Interest rates will still have to rise significantly at a steady pace to reach levels that are sufficiently restrictive, according to \uc2 ECB\uc2  monetary statement.\par \par \uc2 European equities plunged 3.5% on Thursday, while S&P 500 index dropped 2.5%.\par \par \uc2 Major central banks staying on course on hawkish messaging at a time when data is weak is prompting concerns on the growth outlook. U.S. retail sales and factory production in November fell short of expectations, data showed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee forward premiums were broadly unchanged with the 1-year implied yield hovering near the 2% level. Indian equities added to Thursday's losses, while Brent crude futures dipped marginally. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Dhanya Ann Thoppil) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-16T06:04:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221216eicg00mlx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
