\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging markets'  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves burn apace in race to defend  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2022\par 09:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE/NEW YORK, Oct 19 (Reuters) - Emerging markets have been consuming their stockpiles of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves this year at a faster pace than in previous bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness as central banks fight to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the mighty U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 China, which holds the world's largest total \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in excess of $3 trillion, drew down $195 billion from January to August this year, according to \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 This was more than six times the $30 billion it depleted over the same period in 2018, during the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's previous tightening cycle. During another strong dollar phase in 2014, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $61 billion from March to October.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of central banks are facing that extremely difficult choice right now, when their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are depreciating against the dollar," said Ana Jelenkovic, sovereign strategist of the emerging markets group at Marathon Asset Management, referring to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 "Do they let that be the buffer, do they let that absorb the shock? Or do you use some of your assets, reserve buffers, if you think this is just sort of a temporary shock?"\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had fallen by $71 billion by August this year, while Brazil lost $29 billion by September.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, during 2014's dollar strength, both countries had recorded an increase in their reserves in the eight months to October.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is down almost 10% against the dollar this year. While Brazil's reserves have also fallen, it has seen its real rise about 5%, supported by one of the highest reserves to short-term external debt ratios among emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, the stark drawdowns in reserves this year - which are calculated in U.S. dollars - could partially be attributed to valuation effects. The surging U.S. dollar has knocked many \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to multi-year lows, with the euro down 13% year-to-date, sterling down 16% and the yen more than 20% lower.\par \par \uc2 "(Central banks) also invest their reserves in other non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... so you have that kind of translation impact," said Yan Wang, chief emerging markets and China strategist at Alpine Macro. "That's at least a part of the reason why reserves are falling."\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  calculated that on a six-month moving average, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves across emerging markets fell by $21.2 billion in September on an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  valuation-adjusted basis. The unadjusted drop is a bigger $85.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 OUT OF THE BOX\par \par \uc2 The pace at which \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have been used up has prompted some policymakers to use creative methods in the face of a hawkish \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and towering dollar.\par \par \uc2 China's state banks sold a high volume of dollars to buy yuan, but used swaps to procure dollars, banking sources told Reuters. Both onshore and offshore yuan have weakened around 12% year-to-date .\par \par \uc2 Similarly, to conserve reserves, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both the spot and forward markets through state-run banks.\par \par \uc2 Policy makers in countries from the Czech Republic to Chile have been stepping in to shore up \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in addition to rate hikes this year.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, analysts say there is no need to sound the alarm over the declines in reserves.\par \par \uc2 "This is precisely what reserves are for. They're definitely going to replenish reserves when it comes to better times," said Galvin Chia, an emerging markets strategist at \uc2 NatWest Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The concern, however, would be a more gradual recovery in these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  once the dollar peaks, as central banks soak up incoming flows as they prioritise replenishing their reserves.\par \par \uc2 "That means that even if the dollar cycle turns... a lot of EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not see tremendous upside because the central banks will use that opportunity to rebuild their reserves," said Manik Narain, head of emerging markets strategy at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rae Wee in Singapore, Karin Strohecker in London, Rodrigo Campos in New York and Patturaja Murugaboopathy in Bangalore Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Lincoln Feast) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-19T08:17:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221019eiaj012fd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
