\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 INDIA \highlight\uc2  RUPEE-Rupee ends unchanged amid likely cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2022\par 12:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 17 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended flat on Monday, while its Asian counterparts dropped on recession fears, as the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued supporting the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed unchanged at 82.35 per dollar, having traded in an extremely narrow six paisa range all session.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  was likely selling dollars and receiving forwards through state-run banks as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tries to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 82.40 levels, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The forwards market had been quite "volatile," said a Mumbai-based trader. The USD/INR 1-year forward implied yield dropped to 2.45%, its lowest since November 2011, from 2.55% on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "Earlier they (\uc2 RBI\uc2 ) were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market and spending their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. But by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in forwards, they will not use their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves much, as this is more of a dollar supremacy story," said Sugandha Sachdeva, VP of commodity and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Religare Broking.\par \par \uc2 The overarching trend is still negative for the rupee, but in that we might see some relief because equities are trading positively and crude prices and the dollar index are down, she said, adding the rupee might appreciate a tad in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's continuous presence has been a big support to the rupee as it has been in the market most days since last Monday, when the rupee hit a record low of 82.6825, as per traders.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose for the first time in two months in the week ended Oct. 7, increasing by $204 million over the period to $532.87 billion. Reserves were still down 17% compared to its peak of $642.5 billion last year.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in broader markets, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted major losses after last week's red-hot U.S. inflation print reinforced fears of a global recession on assumptions of aggressive hikes by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi in Mumbai; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-17T11:38:32.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221017eiah01tz2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
