\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cenbank's  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  via forwards may hamper rupee's defence -analysts\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2022\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 17 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (\uc2 RBI\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through forward dollar sales instead of an on-spot basis may undermine its effort to boost the rupee, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Since last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the over-the-counter forward market that lifted the rupee from record lows of 82.6825 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars in spot and conducting buy/sell swaps to shift the delivery of dollars to a future date.\par \par \uc2 A buy/sell swap involves an agreement to buy dollars at the spot date and to sell dollars at a future predetermined rate.\par \par \uc2 The difference between the sell rate and the buy rate is the forward premium.\par \par \uc2 The buy/sell swaps by the \uc2 RBI\uc2  have prompted forward premiums on the rupee to plunge.\par \par \uc2 For instance, the 1-year USD/INR implied yield or the cost of carry has dropped to a 11-year low of 2.45% from an intraday high of over 3.07% on Oct. 10.\par \par \uc2 The fall in forward premiums reduces the cost of carrying or holding dollar positions and leads to higher demand for dollar from importers.\par \par \uc2 For the same level of spot, it is now cheaper for importers to buy dollars for a later date.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 RBI\uc2  reducing cost of carry while wanting to defend the rupee seems counterintuitive," said Abhishek Goenka, founder and CEO of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  advisory firm IFA Global.\par \par \uc2 As to reasons the \uc2 RBI\uc2  may be selling dollars forward and not on spot basis, Goenka said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want its spot dollar sales to impact banking system liquidity, which is perilously close to getting into deficit.\par \par \uc2 Another reason could be that \uc2 RBI\uc2  would be concerned "about the optics of falling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves making headlines every week", Goenka said.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen to $532.9 billion from a peak of $642.5 billion last year.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 RBI\uc2  governor \uc2 Shaktikanta Das\uc2  referred to the divergent views on the exchange rate and the adequacy of India's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, saying, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  does not have any fixed exchange rate in mind and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the fall in premiums also dissuades exporters to sell dollar forward.\par \par \uc2 "A lower forward premium makes it easier to short rupee and disincentivises hedging from exporters," said \uc2 Anindya Banerjee\uc2 , head research - \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rates at \uc2 Kotak Securities\uc2 . (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Neha Arora) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-17T09:39:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221017eiah01bgd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
