\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee likely to open lower as risk aversion boosts dollar; \uc2 RBI\uc2  key\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2022\par 04:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is expected to open weaker on Tuesday, as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  rate outlook dampened demand for risky assets and boosted the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is seen around 82.40-82.45 in early trades, down from 82.32 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the local unit had dropped to a record low of 82.6825, but recouped losses to end flat due to likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI)\uc2 . Still, traders reckoned that the rupee's downtrend remained intact.\par \par \uc2 The market is "still searching for a floor" for the rupee and it looks like "we are not there yet", a Mumbai-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 "If the \uc2 RBI\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...then traders will remain long on USD/INR pair throughout the day", said Ashish Ranade, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury chief manager at Cosmos Bank.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped on Tuesday and the dollar index inched higher to 113.22, heading for its fifth daily advance. The offshore Chinese yuan dropped to 7.1840 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. 10-year yield was seen hovering near to 4%.\par \par \uc2 The likelihood of more large Fed rate hikes was lifting Treasury yields and supporting demand for the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Chicago Fed\uc2  president \uc2 Charles Evans\uc2  said on Monday that he sees the policy rate needing to rise "a bit above" 4.5% by early next year and remaining there, as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes stock.\par \par \uc2 The Fed rate is currently at 3%-3.25% and markets are factoring in that its more than likely that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take it to 3.75%-4% next month.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. inflation data due on Thursday will be key in gauging the outlook for rates at the November and December meeting.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, oil prices, among the reasons that the rupee has struggled, cooled off slightly. Brent crude was hovering near $96 a barrel, having climbed to $98.75 intraday on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Asian shares fell and U.S. equity futures extended losses. Geopolitical concerns heated up after a Russian missile attack on Ukraine killed civilians and knocked out power in cites across the country. KEY INDICATORS: ** One-month non-deliverable rupee forward at 82.80; onshore one-month forward premium at 27.5 paise ** USD/INR NSE Oct futures closed on Monday at 82.5825 ** USD/INR forward premium for October-end at 14.5 paise ** Dollar index up at 113.22 ** Brent crude futures up 0.1% at $96.3 per barrel ** Ten-year U.S. note yield at 3.99% ** SGX Nifty nearest-month futures up 0.1% at 17,239 ** As per NSDL data, foreign investors sold a net $474.3 mln worth of Indian shares on Oct. 7\par \par \uc2 ** NSDL data shows foreign investors bought a net $55.5 mln worth of Indian bonds on Oct. 7 (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi in Mumbai; Editing by Neha Arora) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-11T03:45:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221011eiab00a3x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
