\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in NDF market, monitoring rupee positions - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2022\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 7 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  has been selling dollars in the non-deliverable forward (NDF) market via local banks based in India's GIFT City International Financial Services Centre, as it seeks to support the sliding rupee, traders said.               \par \par \uc2 The rupee has repeatedly hits record lows in recent sessions as the likelihood of more super-sized rate hikes from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  piles pressure on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 RBI\uc2  in the onshore NDF market was confirmed by Treasury officials at two large private sector banks present in the International Financial Services Centre (IFSC) at \uc2 Gujarat International Finance Tec-City\uc2  (GIFT City) in western India.               \par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 RBI\uc2  is also keeping a close watch on positions held by banks in this market, and asking questions," one of the officials said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking at gross as well as net positions.               \par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 RBI\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in NDF and spot as the arbitrage between the two has mostly disappeared. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in one works in the other too."               \par \par \uc2 In the offshore NDF market, USD/INR rates tend to trade at a premium to onshore rates when there is major risk aversion sentiment globally and when the rupee is facing significant downward pressure.               \par \par \uc2 "There is merit in the \uc2 RBI\uc2  ensuring that the forward rates for the rupee are in alignment across markets," said Vivek Kumar, economist at QuantEco Research.               \par \par \uc2 "For the \uc2 RBI\uc2 , the GIFT route is the easiest in terms of accessibility to the NDF market."               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-7T09:50:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221007eia70164p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
