\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee falls to a new all-time low of 82 units per dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 New Delhi, Oct. 7. The Indian rupee fell Friday to a new record low of 82.27 units per dollar in early trade, breaking a new historical barrier of depreciation caused by the revaluation of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The weakening of the Indian rupee (INR) at the open came "as investors bet that strong U.S. jobs data due for release today will keep the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  on its aggressive tightening path to curb inflation," financial consultancy EForex India said in an analysis.\par \par \uc2 The agency also pointed to rising crude oil prices, boosted by OPEC+'s decision to cut production by 2 million barrels per day to counter the downward pressure that has weighed on prices in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 This is one of the worst annual performances in the history of the rupee, which was still below 75 units to the dollar last January and was trading at 63.85 at the beginning of 2018.\par \par \uc2 The depreciation comes amid efforts by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 RBI\uc2 , issuer) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market and protect the rupee from a further fall, noted EForex India, "selling dollars through state-owned banks since the start of the Russia-Ukraine war."\par \par \uc2 The Asian country has maintained a position of neutrality in the conflict, avoiding strongly condemning the Russian invasion and calling for dialogue at the same time, but Indian authorities have repeatedly denounced the economic impact of the conflict.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  decided last Friday to raise interest rates by 50 basis points to 5.9% to address inflationary pressure that is hovering around 7% and will remain elevated at around 6% in the second half of fiscal 2022-23 (between April and March).\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  described the economic situation caused by the strengthening of the dollar and aggressive monetary policy measures in the West as a "storm", while lowering the gross domestic product (GDP) growth forecast for fiscal year 2022-23 to 7%.\par \par \uc2 For its part, the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  yesterday lowered GDP growth forecasts to 6.5%. EFE\par \par \uc2 daa/ig\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221007eia7003pv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
