\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-\uc2 India's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  encouraging state refiners to cut spot dollar buying -sources\b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par 11:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 RBI\uc2  not responding to request for comment)\par \par \uc2 By Nidhi Verma and Ira Dugal\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is encouraging state-run refiners to reduce dollar buying in the spot market to contain a sharp fall in the rupee, two sources said, adding they have been asked to lean on a special credit line instead.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  has ensured $9 billion has been made available at overseas branches of some Indian banks for the country's three state-run refiners to tap, said the sources who have direct knowledge of the matter, adding that the funds are available at market rates.\par \par \uc2 "Since last 2-3 days \uc2 RBI\uc2  has been asking companies to tap this credit line," one of the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The credit line is available only for \uc2 Indian Oil Corp\uc2  , \uc2 Hindustan Petroleum Corp\uc2  and \uc2 Bharat Petroleum Corp\uc2 , which together control more than half of India's 5 million barrels per day refining capacity.\par \par \uc2 Monthly oil purchases from overseas account for about 30% of India's overall imports.\par \par \uc2 Banks participating in the credit-line scheme include the \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2 , Canara Bank, Bank of Baroda, \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2  and \uc2 Punjab National Bank\uc2 , said one of the sources.\par \par \uc2 The greenback's surge amid sharp interest rate hikes from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  has sent the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling 10% so far this year. \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollar sales to help prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sources declined to be identified as the discussions were private. The \uc2 RBI\uc2 , the state-run refiners and the lenders did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 The rupee strengthened following the Reuters report to a day's high of 81.16 per dollar from 81.54 prior to the report. (Reporting by Nidhi Verma and Ira Dugal; Editing by Edwina Gibbs and Mark Potter) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-30T10:09:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220930ei9u01hbh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
