\par\par \b \uc2 India's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserve adequacy considered while managing volatile rupee - \uc2 RBI\uc2 's Das\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are to maintain macro economic stability and the adequacy of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves is always kept in mind, Governor \uc2 Shaktikanta Das\uc2  said in a policy speech on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a market-driven exchange rate, the governor said, adding that the \uc2 RBI\uc2  did not have a fixed exchange rate in mind and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to curb excess volatility.\par \par \uc2 "The aspect of adequacy of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves is always kept in mind," Das added.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's actions have helped boost investor confidence, which is reflected in the return of capital flows since July, Das pointed out.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve of $537.5 billion as on Sept. 23 compared favourably with most peer economies, the governor highlighted.\par \par \uc2 However, the reserves are down more than $100 billion from the peak of $642.45 billion reached in September last year.\par \par \uc2 Almost 67% of the decline in reserves during the current financial year is due to valuation changes, Das said.\par \par \uc2 The governor's remarks on the exchange rate and reserves comes on the heels of the rupee's swift decline against the dollar in recent session, including to a record low of 81.95.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars regularly to slow the pace of rupee's decline, traders have said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee on Friday was at 81.5450 per U.S. dollar, up from 81.86 in the previous session and almost unchanged from before Das announced the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's policy decision. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-30T07:24:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220930ei9u00vk5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
