\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sterling volatile as PM defends plan, euro drops with inflation data in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2022\par 13:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pound trims declines after 1% fall as PM defends economic plan\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Euro sinks 1%, focus on inflation data\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dollar bounces back, up 0.66%\par \par \uc2 By Joice Alves\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 29 (Reuters) - Sterling and the euro fell on Thursday as Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  defended her government tax-cutting budget, while relief at the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in bond markets faded.\par \par \uc2 Investors also awaited German inflation data.\par \par \uc2 The British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped the most since mid-June on Wednesday after the \uc2 BoE\uc2  announced an emergency bond-buying plan to shore up a gilt market that had been in freefall with the pound. But data showed UK bond liquidity improved only slightly after the \uc2 BoE\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the face of nagging doubts about Britain's economic management and the outlook for global growth, sterling was 0.19% lower at $1.0866 at 1125 GMT, after falling to $1.0764 earlier.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect sterling to remain volatile.\par \par \uc2 "The moves in cable where huge yesterday and while that hasn't been matched today, it makes it difficult to draw strong conclusion above the intra-day direction of the pound," said \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2 , Head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy at Rabobank London.\par \par \uc2 Appearances from \uc2 BoE\uc2  officials \uc2 David Ramsden\uc2 , \uc2 Silvana Tenreyro\uc2  and \uc2 Huw Pill\uc2  later on Thursday will be closely watched, as will an address by finance minister \uc2 Kwasi Kwarteng\uc2  to his Conservative Party on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Sterling is not out of the woods," said DBS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist \uc2 Philip Wee\uc2 . "The \uc2 BoE\uc2  is seen addressing the symptom and not the cause."\par \par \uc2 "The... government has yet to address the credibility of the tax cut plans, which critics see adding to the inflation woes."\par \par \uc2 EURO STRUGGLES\par \par \uc2 The euro trimmed some declines after weakening as much as 1% in earlier London trading. It was last down 0.2% at $0.9720.\par \par \uc2 Data showed euro zone economic sentiment fell sharply and by more than expected in September as confidence dropped among companies and consumers, who are also downbeat about price trends in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The euro had weakened slightly after separate data showed Spain's annual inflation slowed down to 9% in September from 10.5%.\par \par \uc2 Investors will be closely watching German inflation figures due at 1200 GMT for an indication on the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate hike path.\par \par \uc2 "Unless there is a complete surprise it is only going to affect the euro exchange rates marginally though, as the \uc2 ECB\uc2  is signalling very clearly at the moment that it will react to high inflation levels with decisive rate hikes," said \uc2 Esther Reichelt\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in the German state of NRW rose by 1.8% month-on-month in September, the highest monthly spike since March, and were up by 10.1% year-on-year.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the greenback against sterling, the euro and four other peers, flattened at 112.98, but stood not far below its 20-year high of 114.78, after having its worst day since March 2020 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Official pushback is growing stronger, particularly in Asia where Japan, South Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesia have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in financial markets, to varying degrees, to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and asset prices.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, China's offshore yuan bounced about 0.5%to 7.1280 per dollar after Reuters reported state banks have been told to stock up for yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The risk-sensitive Australian dollar sank 0.6% to $0.6485. A new measure of consumer prices showed annual inflation eased a bit from August to July, offering hope that cost pressures might be close to a peak.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Joice Alves, Additional reporting by Kevin Buckland and Tom Westbrook, Editing by Angus MacSwan and Alex Richardson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-29T12:37:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220929ei9t02bev\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
