\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 INDIA \highlight\uc2  RUPEE-Rupee closes marginally higher, \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2022\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee closed slightly higher against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, after a choppy session in which the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely sold dollars to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 81.86 per U.S. dollar, a tad higher than the record closing low of 81.94 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had opened higher at 81.61, but was not able to sustain the gains on dollar buying by foreign banks and oil companies.\par \par \uc2 Intraday, the rupee came close to falling below the record low of 81.95, prompting the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to sell dollars, according to traders. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was confirmed to Reuters by two bankers and one \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage firm.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was in a narrow trading range of 81.90 to 81.93 to the dollar, for more than two hours in afternoon trades.\par \par \uc2 "Once again, the rupee managed to avoid falling below 82," a trader at a private sector bank said.\par \par \uc2 "However, it clearly looks like it is only a matter of time before rupee slips below that level," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The rebound in the dollar index and a renewed selloff in Treasuries, piled pressure on the rupee. The dollar gauge was up 0.5% at 113.36 and the 10-year Treasury yield was up about 15 basis points.\par \par \uc2 U.S. equity futures indicated that the overnight rally was unlikely to sustain. India's equity gauge, the BSE Sensex , fell 0.3% to 56,409.96. The Sensex earlier in the session had climbed to as high as 57,166.14. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Neha Arora) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-29T11:18:35.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220929ei9t020dm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
