\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee at record low, with cenbank likely helping cap slide\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par 07:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was rooted at all-time lows on Wednesday as U.S. yields surged and the greenback strengthened, with traders suspecting that the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was keeping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening further.\par \par \uc2 The rupee declined 0.37% to 81.88 per dollar by 0511 GMT, having touched a record low of 81.9350 during the session.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to be selling dollars via state-run banks at 81.90 levels, traders told Reuters, helping prevent a drop to 82-per-dollar levels.\par \par \uc2 Appetite for the dollar grew, while risk sentiment was tarnished as global markets sold off heavily on worries over high interest rates causing a recession after a chorus of \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  officials overnight stuck to a hawkish tone to bring down inflation at home.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be a temporary fix as there are heavy dollar bids in the market", a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee could even weaken to 82.50 by the middle of October, he added, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy decision at the end of this month was unlikely to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than a couple of days.\par \par \uc2 On the day, benchmark 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields topped 4%, fuelling further gains in the dollar. Two-year Treasury yields were steady at 4.287%, having touched a 15-year peak earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index rocketed 0.5% to a new two-decade high of 114.650.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are completely dollar bullish. With near-term U.S. yields rising so fast, investors seem to be pricing in for a recession soon," said Anil Bhansali, head of treasury at Finrex Treasury Advisors.\par \par \uc2 Indian equities had a choppy session, as they recovered some of their earlier losses to trade down 0.4%, while benchmark government bond yields rose 4 basis points to 7.3376%. (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi in Mumbai; Editing by Savio D'Souza) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-28T06:38:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220928ei9s00s35\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
