\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India's \uc2 RBI\uc2  may need to tap old ways to boost  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves - economists\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2022\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 Nomura\uc2 's comments)\par \par \uc2 By Anushka Trivedi\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 27 (Reuters) -\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  may have to resort to tried and tested measures to shore up its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, including encouraging non-resident Indians to deposit more funds, as it looks to stabilise a steadily declining rupee, economists said.\par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened 9.5% so far this year, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defending the rupee via dollar sales that depleted its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $545 billion from the peak $642 billion a year ago.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure that a falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not eclipse \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fundamentals," \uc2 Abheek Barua\uc2 , chief economist at \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2 , wrote in a note this week.\par \par \uc2 While there might be some benefits of a depreciated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in closing the trade gap, the damage to the capital account in terms of reduced confidence of investors will outweigh it, he added.\par \par \uc2 According to Barua, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to think of ways to bulk up its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, should the pool shrink to near $500 billion in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "More capital is needed at this stage to stabilise the rupee and enable the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to replenish its reserves chest," he said.\par \par \uc2 Japanese investment house \uc2 Nomura\uc2  said in a note that Asian central banks and governments have in the past relied on certain measures to shore up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and may need to reconsider these as a second line of defence.\par \par \uc2 In India's case, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  had previously tried to halt the pace of capital outflows, ease norms around external commercial borrowings and introduce non-resident deposit schemes, among others, which could be useful to help with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation pressures, \uc2 Nomura\uc2  added.\par \par \uc2 In July, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  had allowed banks to raise foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  non-resident deposits at higher costs and permitted foreign investors to buy shorter term local debt as a way to encourage more inflows.\par \par \uc2 Those measures have only helped marginally, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should explore other options such as those in 2013 when the rupee came under pressure due to the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  announcing plans to taper bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 It may be time to think yet again of the taper tantrum playbook, subsidize forwards and get lumpy non-resident deposits in, Barua said.\par \par \uc2 "NRIs are sensitive to India's robust fundamentals and could be persuaded to deposit their dollars... at attractive rates," he added. (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi in Mumbai) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-27T10:51:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220927ei9r01f2y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
