\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee falls to 81.69 units per dollar and sets new all-time low\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 New Delhi, Sep 26. The Indian rupee fell Monday to a new historic low at 81.69 units per dollar after several consecutive days marking records of depreciation, amid growing fears of a global recession.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee (INR) has depreciated by nearly 10 percent so far this year, losing more than seven units since January, plunged in a context of four years of depreciation.\par \par \uc2 Today's fall marks a considerable drop of 0.86 percent from the previous day, from the 80.99 units per dollar at which it was exchanged at the close of trading last Friday, when for the first time it was on the verge of 81.\par \par \uc2 The rise of the dollar, the depreciation of the pound sterling in the face of speculations of a new economic plan in the United Kingdom, and the fall of the euro, are some of the factors of the economic climate that put pressure on the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, "Asian stock indices fell in early trade today following a sharp drop in U.S. stocks on Friday amid growing concerns of an impending recession in the wake of rising interest rates," financial consultancy EForex India said in its analysis.\par \par \uc2 Given this, the market remains expectant that the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 RBI\uc2 , issuer) "will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through dollar sales to protect the rupee from a sharp depreciation against the dollar," the consultancy said.\par \par \uc2 Other global and domestic factors have also contributed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation for months, affected in part by rising international oil prices, and high inflation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2 , in its monthly bulletin on the performance of the economy, indicated that inflation remains above 6 percent, above the tolerance level, "underscoring the need for monetary policy to keep second-order effects contained and inflation expectations firmly anchored."\par \par \uc2 India's international reserves have also seen a decline in their levels to $545.652 billion according to the balance sheet published last Friday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which corresponds to the previous week, the lowest figure since October 2020. EFE\par \par \uc2 igr/mt/ads\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220926ei9q006up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
