\par\par \b \uc2 Marketmind: Asia's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  doom loops\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2022\par 22:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Reuters) - A look at the day ahead in Asian markets from Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 Expect an ugly open to Asian markets on Monday as investors try to shield themselves from the fallout from the widespread selling that battered stocks, bonds, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The historic rout in UK bonds and sterling took center stage on Friday but at the heart of the gloom shrouding world markets is the Fed's drive to raise rates far higher than most people had bargained for, and the effect that is having on global rates.\par \par \uc2 And the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's 'wrecking ball' status is being painfully felt in Asia, where several \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have sunk to multi-year or record lows, and central banks have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and stop the rot.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rupee hit a record low, Indonesia's rupiah and China's yuan fell to their weakest levels since mid-2020, the Thai baht slumped to a 16-year low, and South Korea's won hit a 13-year trough.\par \par \uc2 Falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  increase inflationary pressures, forcing policymakers to turn more hawkish, tightening financial conditions, and crushing demand. Central banks will find it hard to break this doom loop.\par \par \uc2 Their pool of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  purposes is also limited - even the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will be aware its $1.3 trillion stash won't last forever if it follows last week's historic dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  often enough.\par \par \uc2 And talking of doom loops, if Asian central banks sell chunks of their U.S. Treasuries holdings to support their domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , U.S. yields rise, Treasuries are more attractive, investors pile in, and the dollar strengthens.\par \par \uc2 Asia's economic and corporate calendars on Monday are light.\par \par \uc2 A batch of Japanese economic data, including retail sales and consumer confidence, and China's September PMIs will give an insight into the health of the region's two largest economies at the end of the week.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces its latest interest rate decision on Friday too.\par \par \uc2 Key developments that could provide more direction to markets on Monday:\par \par \uc2 German Ifo (September)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jamie NcGeever in Orlando, Fla.; Editing by Alistair Bell) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-25T20:04:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220925ei9p00q5p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
