\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cenbank may slow  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in Oct-Mar to allow weakness in rupee -\uc2 Kotak Bank\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2022\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The \uc2 RBI\uc2  may slow its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the rupee during October-March, and allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move in alignment with global trends, \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee dropped to a record low of 81.2250 to the dollar on Friday, prompting the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to sell dollars to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the INR to remain under pressure as markets continue to assess the extent of spill-overs from the (U.S.) Fed's hardening policy stance," Upasna Bhardwaj, senior economist at \uc2 Kotak\uc2 , said in a note.\par \par \uc2 For several months, the \uc2 Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently stepped in to aid the rupee, as the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's aggressive rate hikes dampen demand for non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In July alone, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  sold $19 billion dollars, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin.\par \par \uc2 Alongside its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forward dollar holdings fell to $22 billion from $64 billion in April.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to become more prudent in 2H FY23, while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Bhardwaj said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have dropped to near $550 billion from a peak of almost $642 billion.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffer was sufficient to shield the economy against any major external shock, and the \uc2 RBI\uc2  may opt for "restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", Bhardwaj said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inclusion in the global bond indices may push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  temporarily higher above 79 per dollar, but Bhardwaj reckons it will be temporary, as the \uc2 RBI\uc2  would like to rebuild the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffer and avert further over-valuation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She expects rupee to trade in a 79-83 rupee per dollar band for the rest of the current fiscal year. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Neha Arora)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-26T09:01:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220923ei9n016tp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
