\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA RUPEE-Rupee marks worst week in 1-1/2 years, traders point to \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2022\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee steadied by the close of trading on Friday after a turbulent week when it tumbled past 81 per dollar to a record low, with traders pointing to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid fall.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 80.99 per dollar, against a previous close of 80.86. It fell to a low of 81.2250 during the session before the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders at state-run banks told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted its worst week since April last year, shedding 1.6% with most of the losses in the past two trading sessions.\par \par \uc2 "There was probably heavy selling at 80.97 levels. On last days of the week, it's usually either \uc2 RBI\uc2  trying to stymie the fall or there are genuine inflows in bulk," said Ashish Ranade, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury chief manager at Cosmos Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Overall, it's a very difficult task for the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to control the rupee's depreciation. We're now positioning for a 80.75-81.25 trading range, with the higher end acting as tough resistance for the USD/INR pair."\par \par \uc2 The dollar index has soared to two-decade highs and risk assets have been battered since the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  late on Wednesday hiked interest rates and took a hawkish stance to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 India's equities sank 1.7% on Friday as the selloff in Asian markets continued. Benchmark bond yields , too, jumped 8 basis points to 7.3926%.\par \par \uc2 Focus now shifts to the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's meeting next week, with its decision due on Friday. With inflation accelerating and the rupee depreciating, a hike is guaranteed, but markets are split on the consensus.\par \par \uc2 Only a slim majority of economists in a Reuters poll expect a 50 basis point hike, while some others see a smaller 35 bps rise.\par \par \uc2 However, several large foreign banks such as Standard Chartered, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  and \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  have revised their call to a half-point rate increase. (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi in Mumbai; Editing by Saumyadeb Chakrabarty) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-23T11:16:51.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220923ei9n01jh9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
