\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-INDIA RUPEE-Rupee hits record low as Asian peers tumble on Fed rate view\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds chart to show rupee's fall)\par \par \uc2 By Nimesh Vora\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee dropped to a record low versus the U.S. dollar on Thursday, as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined on concerns over the pace and quantum of \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's policy tightening ahead.\par \par \uc2 The rupee closed at a record low of 80.86 to the dollar, down from 79.9750 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 It was the biggest single-day fall for the local unit since Feb. 24.\par \par \uc2 Traders that Reuters spoke to, were unable to confirm whether the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market during the session.\par \par \uc2 Some traders said the \uc2 RBI\uc2  may have stepped in to arrest the rupee's decline, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not too aggressive.\par \par \uc2 However, most traders Reuters spoke to could not confirm if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market during the session. Traders at two state-run banks denied that \uc2 RBI\uc2  sold dollars to rein-in the rupee's fall.\par \par \uc2 All through the session, the rupee remained under pressure after the Fed sprung a hawkish outlook.\par \par \uc2 While the Fed's 75 basis-point rate hike was on expected lines, financial markets were surprised by the hawkish so-called dot plot.\par \par \uc2 The dot plot indicated that the rates will reach 4.4% by the end of this year, which would mean a cumulative increase of 125 basis points over the remaining two meetings in November and December.\par \par \uc2 Further, policymakers see rates rising to 4.6% by end-2023.\par \par \uc2 On the back of these forecasts, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged and equities declined.\par \par \uc2 "Given the current pro-dollar and weak equity sentiment, we expect \uc2 RBI\uc2  to... focus on smoothening the move towards 81 over the next few sessions," said Gautam Kumar, head of financial products at Kristal.AI, a Singapore-based digital private wealth management platform.\par \par \uc2 "We think USD/INR will just shift to trade in a higher 80-82 range over the medium term."\par \par \uc2 The dollar index at one point reached a fresh 20-year high of 111.80, but came off as the Japanese yen jumped after authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 1998.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Neha Arora and Dhanya Ann Thoppil) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-22T12:02:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220922ei9m01xtx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
