\par\par \b \uc2 India's  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  reserves near 2-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2022\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 12 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped to their lowest since October 2020, as the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 proactively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to aid the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of a surging dollar, analysts said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped to $553.1 billion in the week ended Sept. 2, a decline of almost $8 billion from the previous week, according to data released by the \uc2 RBI\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 It was the biggest drawdown in reserves since early July.\par \par \uc2 In the week ended Sept. 2, the rupee had fallen to a record low of 80.12 against the dollar on prospects of aggressive monetary tightening by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 RBI\uc2  Governor \uc2 Shaktikanta Das\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will anchor expectations around the depreciating rupee and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent an overshoot, ensuring the exchange rate reflects fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Kumar, an economist at QuantEco Research, pointed out that not all of the decline in reserves was due to \uc2 RBI\uc2  spot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  mark-to-market and maturity of forward contracts would have likely contributed to the fall, Kumar said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  has been regularly dipping into the reserves to shield the rupee from the volatility fuelled by U.S. Fed's rate hikes and high commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index and short-term Treasury yields have climbed to multi-year highs.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 RBI\uc2  might as well hang on with the current strategy for a little bit longer and hope the commodity price softening continues and the dollar does not find any incremental reasons to strengthen," Kumar said. (Reporting by Anushka Trivedi and Nimesh Vora; Editing by Neha Arora) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-12T07:29:11.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220912ei9c00n2m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
