\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee likely flat on dollar pullback, oil surge\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2022\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is tipped to open flat to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after oil prices scaled to a one-month high and as the dollar index retreated.\par \par \uc2 In early trade, the rupee is expected around the same level of 79.9625 from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The unit fell to a record low of 80.12 on Monday before slipping back above the psychological level of 80 on likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oil prices "back on upward trajectory" is an issue for the rupee, a trader at a Mumbai-based bank said.\par \par \uc2 "However, if the rupee after all the negative cues still managed to hold above 80 yesterday, then there is little reason to chase the pair (USD/INR) higher."\par \par \uc2 The Brent crude futures contract jumped 4% on Monday, its best session in six weeks, on prospects of OPEC+ supply cuts.\par \par \uc2 Brent is now hovering near $104.50 a barrel, a sizeable recovery from its recent low of around $91.50.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index held its ground near 108.80, down from a 20-year peak of 109.48. The slight pullback on the dollar index came amid a recovery in the euro.\par \par \uc2 The euro, which was supported by expectations that the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could opt for a 75-basis-point rate hike, rose to near parity to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The slight moderation in risk aversion further weighed on demand for the safe-haven dollar.\par \par \uc2 Near-term Treasury yields were hovering near their highest levels since 2007. The focus this week will be on the U.S. ISM manufacturing and non-manufacturing data and the monthly jobs report.\par \par \uc2 The jobs report on Friday and the U.S. consumer inflation report due next week will be instrumental in shaping expectations on whether the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  hikes rate by 50 basis points or 75 basis points next month.\par \par \uc2 KEY INDICATORS:\par \par \uc2 ** One-month non-deliverable rupee forward at 80.16; onshore one-month forward premium at 21.51 paise\par \par \uc2 ** Dollar index up at 108.85\par \par \uc2 ** Brent crude futures at $104.4 per barrel\par \par \uc2 ** Ten-year U.S. note yield at 3.10%\par \par \uc2 ** SGX Nifty nearest-month futures up 0.3% at 17,438\par \par \uc2 ** As per NSDL data, foreign investors sold a net $14.2mln worth of Indian shares on Aug. 26\par \par \uc2 ** NSDL data shows foreign investors bought a net $19.9mln worth of Indian bonds on Aug. 26\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Sherry Jacob-Phillips) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-8-30T03:52:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220830ei8u009sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
