\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises on dollar sales by exporters\b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2022\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was trading higher versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as exporters sold dollars, allowing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to withstand a rise in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was trading at a session-high of 79.7100 per U.S. dollar at 0514 GMT, compared with 79.8625 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has been hovering in a narrow trading range just above the 80 level, thanks to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid deteriorating risk sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "The range for the day, as \uc2 RBI\uc2  ensures to keep the rupee within 80 levels, is 79.70 to 80.00," said Anil Bhansali, head treasury at Finrex Treasury Advisors.\par \par \uc2 "Exporters may keep selling (dollars) above 79.90, while importers may buy any good dips (on USD/INR pair) they get."\par \par \uc2 The rupee has managed to avoid reaching a new record low despite the broader dollar index surging to 109 from 105 in the last two weeks. A combination of foreign equity inflows and \uc2 RBI\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bets have helped the rupee.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude futures climbed almost 4% on Tuesday. Higher oil prices tend to hurt the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as India is a large importer of crude.\par \par \uc2 Traders reckon Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's comments on Friday at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  symposium in Jackson Hole, Wyoming could push the rupee out its narrow trading range.\par \par \uc2 "At Jackson Hole, the Fed is likely to emphasize its commitment to price stability, even at the risk of recession," BofA Securities said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Powell is likely to say the pace of hikes could slow, while emphasizing restrictive policy and no quick pivot to cuts."\par \par \uc2 India's main stocks gauge, the BSE Sensex, was almost flat after opening lower. (Reporting by Nimesh Vora; Editing by Saumyadeb Chakrabarty) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-8-24T06:45:50.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220824ei8o00qe1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
