\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's twin deficits may overwhelm \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2022\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Aug 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record trade deficit in July has raised considerable concerns over its external balances and might force the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rethink its strategy of persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rupee's depreciation.\par \par \uc2 The preliminary trade deficit widened nearly three-fold from a year earlier to $31.02 billion, due to a slump in exports and higher imports.\par \par \uc2 This has prompted banks to raise their forecasts for the current account deficit (CAD), reviving bearish sentiment towards the INR.\par \par \uc2 Nomura\uc2 , for instance, expects the CAD to rise to 3.3% of gross domestic product for the financial year ending in March 2023, from 1.2% in FY2022.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over India's ability to fund a widening CAD will intensify pressure on the INR.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves shrinking by $60 billion since March, largely due to the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may want to step back and let the exchange rate be determined by market forces in the short term.\par \par \uc2 This approach does run the risk of exacerbating the CAD as further INR weakness may reverse nascent foreign institutional investor inflows to India's stock markets.\par \par \uc2 But it could save valuable reserves, while allowing lower oil prices and declining \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields to ultimately turn sentiment in the rupee's favour.\par \par \uc2 USD/INR is likely to consolidate in a broad 78.00-80.00 range. Trading these parameters with protective stops below 77.90 and above 80.20 would be prudent.\par \par \uc2 See \uc2 RBI\uc2  policy meeting preview For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Krishna Kumar is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own. Editing by Sonali Desai)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-8-8T03:10:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220805ei8500gwd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
