\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee sees biggest single-day gain in nearly a year\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2022\par 13:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates to add close, milestones)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee posted its biggest single-day gain in nearly a year on Friday, aided by a sharp reversal in the dollar, while bond yields touched their lowest in 2-1/2 months tracking falls in their U.S. counterparts.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields fell overnight after data showed the economy contracted again in the second quarter, suggesting that the Fed may not need to be so aggressive with rate hikes to cool inflation.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended trading at 79.25 against the dollar, 0.6% stronger than Thursday's close of 79.7550 and its best single-day performance since Aug. 27 last year.\par \par \uc2 It touched a session high of 79.17, its strongest since July 7.\par \par \uc2 "The recent correction lower in commodity prices is providing some respite to the INR, albeit likely only temporarily," Kunal Kundu, India economist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  wrote in a note published Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Growing market conviction that a U.S. recession is on the way and consequent safe-haven demand for the dollar are key near-term risks for rupee. The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue to limit rupee volatility," he added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has zero tolerance for volatile movements in the rupee and will continue to engage with the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ensure the rupee finds its appropriate level, its chief \uc2 Shaktikanta Das\uc2  said last week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar languished near a six-week low against the yen amid a sharp retreat in Treasury yields. Almost all Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 10-year bond yield ended trading at 7.3196%, after falling to 7.2527% earlier, its lowest since May 12. It had ended at 7.3316% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 India's stock markets and ended up 1.35% and 1.25%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Foreign fund flows will be a crucial factor determining the rupee's fortunes in the coming months. Foreign investors have been net sellers of Indian stocks worth more than $30 billion so far in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Traders will now shift their focus to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's monetary policy review next week.\par \par \uc2 "With the Fed having stuck to a 75 bps hike and concerns of a global recession still looming, the \uc2 RBI\uc2  may announce a modest 25-35 bps increase in the repo rate next week," a senior trader at a private bank said.\par \par \uc2 "We will see the 10-year move in a 7.20% to 7.35% range until (then)," he added.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said they expect the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's monetary policy committee to vote unanimously for a 35 bps rate hike next week.\par \par \uc2 "While inflation is likely to remain elevated in the near term, we think the MPC may acknowledge that price pressures have peaked, and note the favourable tailwinds by reducing its inflation forecasts, albeit marginally," they added.\par \par \uc2 India's retail inflation remained painfully above the 7% mark and beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance band for the sixth month in a row in June, but has shown an easing bias over recent months. (Editing by Kim Coghill and Uttaresh.V) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-29T12:11:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220729ei7t013w6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
