\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-\uc2 RBI\uc2  may find allies in lower oil, sliding U.S. yields\b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2022\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 July 25 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to slow the Indian rupee's depreciation are likely to draw support from lower oil prices and sliding \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields, which are helping blunt the dollar's advance.\par \par \uc2 U.S. crude prices closed below $95 a barrel on Friday while benchmark 10-year Treasury yields dropped to an eight-week low on rising fears of a global recession.\par \par \uc2 Elevated prices for crude oil, which forms a large chunk of India's import bill, have pushed up the trade deficit while the current account gap has widened as rising U.S. interest rates triggered an exodus of foreign institutional investors from Indian stock markets. The widening twin deficits are negating the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's efforts to stem the INR decline.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have shrunk by a sizable $70 billion since early September - $60 billion of the drop occurring since March - largely due to the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Despite the dollar sales, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been unable to prevent the INR from falling 7% this year to a record low of 80.18.\par \par \uc2 The more favourable moves in oil and Treasury yields and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purported intent to spend another $100 billion to defend the rupee could act as catalysts for a long-overdue USD/INR pullback.\par \par \uc2 USD/INR will encounter strong resistance at 80.10-20, and a drift lower towards initial support at 79.40-50 is likely.\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Krishna Kumar is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own. Editing by Sonali Desai)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-28T03:10:28.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220725ei7p00eql\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
