\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian rupee snaps 11-week losing streak as \uc2 RBI\uc2  steps in\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2022\par 12:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates with details, closing levels)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee snapped a 11-week losing streak on Friday, benefiting from \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it fell through the 80-per-dollar mark.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 79.8550 slightly stronger compared to its close of 79.9450 on Thursday and also marginally above last Friday's close of 79.8775.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has zero tolerance for volatile and bumpy movements in the rupee and will continue to engage with the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ensure the rupee finds its appropriate level, its chief \uc2 Shaktikanta Das\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee touched a lifetime low of 80.0650 on Tuesday but heavy dollar sales from state-run banks on behalf of the \uc2 RBI\uc2  has helped limit further losses in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 Indian bond yields edged lower on Friday, tracking their U.S. peers' slide after a bigger-than-expected hike by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ) brought the focus back onto a possible global recession.\par \par \uc2 India's benchmark 10-year bond yield ended trading at 7.41% compared to its close of 7.44% on Thursday. On the week, the 10-year yield fell 2 basis points.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields fell on Thursday, with the benchmark 10-year note below 2.9%, weighed by soft economic data and after the \uc2 ECB\uc2 's first interest rate hike in 11 years.\par \par \uc2 Traders said Indian bond yields had been trading in a tight band amid mixed global triggers and the upcoming monetary policy review in early-August.\par \par \uc2 DBS said in a note that despite recent signs suggesting inflation may have peaked, it was premature to go easy on inflation as a past \uc2 RBI\uc2  study had shown that a 5% depreciation in the rupee versus their baseline projection could push inflation higher by roughly 20 basis points and vice versa.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2 's baseline rupee projection was at 76 per dollar as per the monetary policy report published in April.\par \par \uc2 "This also explains the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preference to anchor the exchange rate so as not to aggravate supply-side price pressures," \uc2 Radhika Rao\uc2 , an economist with DBS said.\par \par \uc2 DBS now expects a 35 basis points increase in the key rate by the \uc2 RBI\uc2  at its August meeting versus 50 bps earlier. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Uttaresh.V and Alison Williams) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-22T11:30:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220722ei7m01lhh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
