\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 2-Indian rupee holds below 80 a dollar mark, \uc2 RBI\uc2  hand suspected\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2022\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats with no change in text)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was held below the 80-per-dollar mark on Wednesday aided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said, while gains in the domestic share market and a fall in global crude oil prices also helped.\par \par \uc2 The euro held near two-week highs versus the dollar on expectations of a bigger \uc2 ECB\uc2  interest rate increase this week than earlier anticipated and a Reuters report that a key Russian gas pipeline would reopen on time after maintenance.\par \par \uc2 India's partially convertible rupee ended trading at 79.99 per dollar, weaker compared to its close of 79.94 on Tuesday, when it had hit a record low of 80.0650.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the pair to trade in the range of 79.80-80.10 this week," economists at \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent runaway depreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 A senior source aware of the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's thinking said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to sell a sixth of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the rupee.\par \par \uc2 Traders said stronger domestic shares helped sentiment, but a reversal of foreign fund buying will be key for the rupee. Foreign investors have sold nearly $30 billion worth of shares since the start of this year.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares rose more than 1% to a six-week high as oil producers and refiners surged after the government slashed windfall taxes on local crude sales and fuel exports.\par \par \uc2 "Until we start seeing inflows into the market, rupee will remain under pressure. Inflows are unlikely to start in a rush," a senior trader at a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 He said movement in global crude oil prices will remain important for bonds and rupee in the interim, as India imports more than two-thirds of its oil needs and higher crude expands the country's trade and account account deficit.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices fell more than $1 a barrel under pressure from global \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to limit inflation and ahead of expected builds in U.S. crude inventories as fuel demand weakens.\par \par \uc2 In the domestic debt market, the benchmark 10-year bond yield ended up 2 basis points at 7.45%. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Raju Gopalakrishnan, Bradley Perrett and Shailesh Kuber) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-20T13:13:26.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220720ei7k024b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
