\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Indian importers feel heat as rupee depreciates over 7%\b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2022\par 13:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, July 19 (Reuters) - India's importers including of crude oil, commodities, chemicals and electrical machinery, besides business travellers and students studying abroad have been hit hard following a sharp depreciation of rupee against the dollar this year. The rupee has depreciated over 7% against dollar this year. On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the rupee steady slightly after the unit weakened to 80.05 per dollar in early trade, a record low for a seventh successive session.\par \par \uc2 Following are key facts about the rupees depreciation:\par \par \uc2 WHY IS THE RUPEE FALLING? Like most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the partially convertible Indian rupee, fell in recent months as risk aversion rose on expectations of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  raising rates to curb inflation, prompting investors to flee riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 A severe dollar shortage ensued after foreign investors made net sales of Indian shares - amounting to more than $30 billion so far in 2022. Fears of widening current and trade account deficits have further hit the rupee.\par \par \uc2 INDIA'S WIDENING TRADE DEFICIT India's overall trade deficit is expected to widen to over $130 billion this fiscal year, driven by global crude oil prices, from $87 billion a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 RISING ENERGY COSTS India meets 85% of its crude oil needs through imports, so the rupee's depreciation has added to the retail cost of petrol, diesel and cooking gas.\par \par \uc2 The weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also hit earnings of power generation companies - forced to resort to costlier coal imports amid a shortfall in domestic coal production. India's energy imports, including crude oil, petroleum products and coal, are expected to rise sharply this year from nearly $194 billion in the fiscal year ending in March 2022, constituting near one-third of total merchandise imports.\par \par \uc2 However, refiners like \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  could benefit thanks to their exports of petroleum products.\par \par \uc2 GOLD IMPORTS Buying gold jewellery has become costlier for millions of Indians due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation and a recent hike in import duty. India's gold imports, the third biggest item after crude oil and electronic imports, crossed $46 billion in 2021/22.\par \par \uc2 HOUSEHOLD ITEMS Hundreds of imported household items including edible oil, dry fruits, medicines, cosmetics, garments, electric appliances, mobiles, kitchenware as well as business travel and foreign education for nearly 1.1 million Indian students have become costlier.\par \par \uc2 RISING MANUFACTURING COSTS\par \par \uc2 The rupee's fall has increased input costs for manufacturers including auto companies, telecom, engineering goods, consumer electronics, food processing and civil aviation. India is a major importer of industrial chemicals, steel, rubber, wooden, glassware and other machinery.\par \par \uc2 The companies are also worried about the rising costs of dollar-denominated debt.\par \par \uc2 WINDFALL FOR GOODS EXPORTERS, IT COMPANIES The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation could prove a windfall for goods and services exporters including IT companies \uc2 Infosys\uc2 , TCS, \uc2 TECH Mahindra\uc2  as their billings are largely in dollars.\par \par \uc2 India's services exports touched nearly $250 billion in 2021/22 fiscal year ending in March, while goods exports touched nearly $420 billion.\par \par \uc2 Pharmaceutical exporters, with over $25 billion annual exports and one-third of sales in the U.S. market, are major beneficiaries, analysts said, while warning about the impact of global slowdown on Indian exporters.\par \par \uc2 India's goods exports grew by nearly 25% to nearly $119 billion during April-June period, from a year period.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Manoj Kumar) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-19T12:43:42.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220719ei7j020dl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
