\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee at record lows, but \uc2 RBI \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  slows slide\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2022\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates with details, new low)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hit record lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after higher oil prices raised concerns of sustained inflation, although intermittent dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped limit losses.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee was trading at 78.75/76 per dollar by 0745 GMT, compared to its close of 78.34 on Monday. The unit touched an all-time low of 78.7750 just earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 India imports more than two-thirds of its oil requirements, and higher crude prices add to the country's trade and current account deficits (CAD) and hurt the rupee by pushing up imported inflation.\par \par \uc2 "With crude rising yet again, we could see rupee head towards 79-79.50 levels in the next week or so depending on what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does," a senior trader at a private bank said.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices rallied for a third day as major producers Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates looked unlikely to be able to boost output significantly, while political unrest in Libya and Ecuador added to supply concerns.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  has been intermittently selling dollars via state-run banks to prevent runaway losses in the rupee, but dollar demand in the system was far stronger.\par \par \uc2 Global dollar funding stress is evident through the widening LIBOR-OIS spread, and in the domestic market, \uc2 RBI\uc2 's heavy forwards market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has compounded the problem of cash dollar shortage, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  has been selling forward dollars to avoid infusing rupee liquidity in the system and that has led to the one-year onshore forward dollar premiums collapsing to below 3%.\par \par \uc2 "Dislocation in forward rates, falling \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  cover, persistently high commodity prices, limited exchange rate pass-through to inflation and elevated INR valuations may call for the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to re-orient its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy," said \uc2 Madhavi Arora\uc2 , an economist at \uc2 Emkay Global\uc2 . "Allowing INR to gently weaken over time is the right strategy, giving CAD space to improve," she added.\par \par \uc2 Jigar Trivedi, a research analyst at \uc2 Anand Rathi\uc2  Shares and Stock Brokers, said he expects the rupee to depreciate towards 80-81 per dollar levels by the year-end weighed down by the twin deficits and rising interest rate differentials.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Amy Caren Daniel) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-28T08:48:32.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220628ei6s0119p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
