\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to defend rupee - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2022\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, May 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold $700 million dollars to prop up the rupee on Thursday as it plunged to a record low, according to three traders, amid broad based selling in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell as much as 0.5% to 77.63 to the dollar, its second record low in less than a week.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  both in the spot and the futures market when the rupee hit 77.55-77.60, the traders, who did not want to be identified, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Reuters reported \uc2 RBI\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through the week and the official said it will do so again if volatility persists without targeting any particular level.\par \par \uc2 The official said that it does not like "jerky" movements of over 0.50 Indian rupees against the dollar in one day.\par \par \uc2 Traders said \uc2 RBI\uc2  has sold $2 billion to $3 billion worth of dollars since the start of the week to defend the rupee.\par \par \uc2 RBI\uc2  did not immediately reply to a message seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RBI\uc2  has foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of about $597.7 billion, which it sees as a formidable stockpile to defend the rupees.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 RBI\uc2  is showing intent in reducing rupee volatility," one of the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee pared some of its early losses after the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade at 77.46 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under pressure due to concerns over rising inflation, traders said.\par \par \uc2 India's March retail inflation rose to a 17-month high of 6.95% and April data is expected later in the day. (Reporting by Savio Shetty in Mumbai, Aftab Ahmed and Nidhi Verma in New Delhi; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-5-12T11:04:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220512ei5c01xtx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
